1
00:00:08,049 --> 00:00:09,426
I had never seen…

2
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:15,140
a drink in my hand freeze
in real time before.

3
00:00:15,223 --> 00:00:17,225
MIDWINTER

4
00:00:19,644 --> 00:00:21,980
It was incredibly cold.

5
00:00:22,063 --> 00:00:23,440
My hands are so cold.

6
00:00:24,232 --> 00:00:25,692
<i>My whole body was cold.</i>

7
00:00:26,901 --> 00:00:28,361
<i>It felt so reckless.</i>

8
00:00:30,113 --> 00:00:31,614
It was impossible. It was just…

9
00:00:31,698 --> 00:00:32,532
SNOWY MOUNTAIN

10
00:00:32,615 --> 00:00:33,491
<i>It was so cold.</i>

11
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:35,118
<i>I was dazed there.</i>

12
00:00:35,201 --> 00:00:36,244
TARZZAN GROANS

13
00:00:36,327 --> 00:00:37,912
<i>I couldn't even close my hand.</i>

14
00:00:38,830 --> 00:00:41,583
I took off my glove for a moment,
and my hand froze.

15
00:00:42,584 --> 00:00:45,837
SUFFERING

16
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,630
This is so bad.

17
00:00:47,714 --> 00:00:50,633
-Your leg?
-Here. It feels like it's being torn.

18
00:00:52,010 --> 00:00:53,428
<i>I felt so weak.</i>

19
00:00:53,511 --> 00:00:56,264
I was like, "If viewers criticize me
for this, so be it.

20
00:00:56,347 --> 00:00:58,141
It's killing me."

21
00:00:58,224 --> 00:01:00,226
<i>I'd never climbed a mountain before.</i>

22
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:02,479
<i>I felt I wasn't ready, but I had to go on.</i>

23
00:01:05,648 --> 00:01:07,484
BEGINNER HIKERS'

24
00:01:07,567 --> 00:01:11,863
K-HIKING CHALLENGE

25
00:01:18,369 --> 00:01:22,582
TAKE A HIKE!

26
00:01:23,917 --> 00:01:24,876
Hiking…

27
00:01:25,877 --> 00:01:28,254
Why do you think people go hiking?

28
00:01:29,881 --> 00:01:31,090
Did you find an answer?

29
00:02:01,788 --> 00:02:04,165
DECEMBER, 2025

30
00:02:04,791 --> 00:02:08,169
NEAR NAMSAN, SEOUL

31
00:02:09,629 --> 00:02:11,714
THE DAY OF THE MEMBERS' FIRST MEETING

32
00:02:11,798 --> 00:02:14,801
SININA

33
00:02:14,884 --> 00:02:19,055
THE MEMBERS DON'T KNOW ANYTHING
ABOUT THE PROGRAM YET

34
00:02:20,223 --> 00:02:21,933
Why do I feel so nervous?

35
00:02:23,434 --> 00:02:26,437
SOMEONE ARRIVES EARLY, FEELING NERVOUS

36
00:02:28,314 --> 00:02:32,360
THE FIRST MEMBER ENTERS

37
00:02:32,443 --> 00:02:33,653
Someone's here.

38
00:02:33,736 --> 00:02:35,655
-Hello.
-You scared me.

39
00:02:35,738 --> 00:02:37,991
THIS YOUNG MAN APPEARING
WITH AN INNOCENT SMILE IS…

40
00:02:38,074 --> 00:02:40,994
TARZZAN (REAL NAME: LEE CHAE-WON)

41
00:02:41,077 --> 00:02:43,830
THE OLDEST MEMBER OF ALLDAY PROJECT

42
00:02:47,709 --> 00:02:49,752
AN ALL-ROUND ARTIST WITH A COLORFUL CAREER

43
00:02:49,836 --> 00:02:52,755
BUT THE REAL LEE CHAE-WON
IS AS CUTE AS A MONKEY

44
00:02:53,339 --> 00:02:54,883
What are you holding?

45
00:02:54,966 --> 00:02:57,886
-Our new album's been released.
-Oh, your album?

46
00:02:57,969 --> 00:02:59,095
Thank you.

47
00:02:59,178 --> 00:03:01,723
HE BROUGHT HIS ALBUMS AS GIFTS
FOR THE FIRST MEETING

48
00:03:01,806 --> 00:03:04,183
-Have you been well?
-Have you lost weight?

49
00:03:04,267 --> 00:03:06,519
I have, after the album release.

50
00:03:06,603 --> 00:03:07,729
-Is that so?
-Yes.

51
00:03:08,354 --> 00:03:09,898
-His group's new album.
-Right.

52
00:03:09,981 --> 00:03:12,275
A HEARTFELT HANDWRITTEN LETTER

53
00:03:12,358 --> 00:03:15,194
No, don't read it here.
It's so embarrassing.

54
00:03:15,904 --> 00:03:17,947
HE'S SHYER THAN HE LOOKS

55
00:03:18,698 --> 00:03:20,742
He wrote that he'd do his best.

56
00:03:20,825 --> 00:03:23,119
WHATEVER IT MAY BE, HE'S ENTHUSIASTIC

57
00:03:23,202 --> 00:03:25,496
Did you guess who else would come?

58
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:28,041
Well, I couldn't even guess.

59
00:03:28,124 --> 00:03:30,543
So when I was told
to open the door earlier,

60
00:03:31,669 --> 00:03:33,755
I thought,
"What if some people are already here?"

61
00:03:35,173 --> 00:03:36,758
"What should I do, then?"

62
00:03:36,841 --> 00:03:38,968
I hadn't been this nervous in a while.

63
00:03:39,052 --> 00:03:41,054
THE MEMBERS DON'T KNOW
WHO THE OTHERS ARE YET

64
00:03:41,638 --> 00:03:43,640
Can I go in and use the bathroom first?

65
00:03:43,723 --> 00:03:45,141
-The bathroom?
-Yes.

66
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:46,893
THE DOOR OPENS RIGHT AWAY

67
00:03:46,976 --> 00:03:48,561
Filming has already started inside.

68
00:03:48,645 --> 00:03:49,479
Really?

69
00:03:49,562 --> 00:03:53,524
HE GOES IN A HURRY TO ANSWER NATURE'S CALL

70
00:03:53,608 --> 00:03:55,526
They'll be here soon. Wait.

71
00:03:59,155 --> 00:04:00,365
Hello.

72
00:04:01,032 --> 00:04:02,367
Hello.

73
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:05,912
CAR, THE GARDEN

74
00:04:06,829 --> 00:04:08,623
-Why are you shy?
-When did you get here?

75
00:04:08,706 --> 00:04:10,667
Why didn't you knock first?

76
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:14,837
AN UNEXPECTED CHARACTER APPEARS
AT AN UNEXPECTED TIME

77
00:04:14,921 --> 00:04:16,089
Hello.

78
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:18,549
We met not long ago.

79
00:04:18,633 --> 00:04:19,467
Really?

80
00:04:20,218 --> 00:04:22,595
-Did you meet?
-We met at 10CM's show.

81
00:04:24,222 --> 00:04:27,517
We were too busy with sound check
to go greet you then.

82
00:04:28,476 --> 00:04:30,645
AS SOON AS HE SITS DOWN…

83
00:04:30,728 --> 00:04:32,522
-By the way…
-What?

84
00:04:32,605 --> 00:04:34,357
-Can I go to the bathroom?
-You can't.

85
00:04:34,857 --> 00:04:36,276
-I'm about to go--
-Seriously, no.

86
00:04:36,359 --> 00:04:37,527
It's urgent.

87
00:04:37,610 --> 00:04:38,444
Then I'll just…

88
00:04:38,528 --> 00:04:40,280
OKAY, YOU CAN GO

89
00:04:40,363 --> 00:04:42,949
CAR, THE GARDEN (REAL NAME: CHA JUNG-WON)

90
00:04:43,032 --> 00:04:45,034
BABY AND ME, HUNGRY!

91
00:04:45,118 --> 00:04:47,203
HIGHLY ACTIVE ON YOUTUBE & VARIETY SHOWS

92
00:04:47,287 --> 00:04:49,497
MAIN JOB: SINGER-SONGWRITER
SECOND JOB: ENTERTAINER

93
00:04:49,580 --> 00:04:53,042
A WELL-LOVED, 14-YEAR VETERAN SINGER

94
00:04:53,126 --> 00:04:56,004
HE HAS RETURNED LOOKING REFRESHED

95
00:04:56,087 --> 00:04:58,715
So what's the age gap between you two?

96
00:04:58,798 --> 00:05:00,258
I was born in 2002.

97
00:05:00,341 --> 00:05:01,509
I was born in 1990.

98
00:05:01,592 --> 00:05:02,677
YEAR OF THE HORSE

99
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:03,761
Twelve years.

100
00:05:03,845 --> 00:05:06,514
I thought
he was younger than that, though.

101
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:09,434
So you can handle much younger?

102
00:05:10,101 --> 00:05:11,519
What is there to handle?

103
00:05:12,145 --> 00:05:13,563
It's just age.

104
00:05:14,522 --> 00:05:16,232
HE'S JUST A GUY WHO'S 12 YEARS YOUNGER

105
00:05:16,316 --> 00:05:18,318
Then what should I call you?

106
00:05:18,401 --> 00:05:19,777
Mr. The Garden?

107
00:05:20,445 --> 00:05:21,279
Whatever you like.

108
00:05:21,362 --> 00:05:23,531
Garden, the garden, or Jung-won, whatever.

109
00:05:23,614 --> 00:05:24,949
-Call him Car-the.
-Car-the.

110
00:05:25,033 --> 00:05:26,367
That's okay, too.

111
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:27,618
Car-the, it is.

112
00:05:27,702 --> 00:05:29,620
SILENCE

113
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:32,248
It'd be nice to learn music from you.

114
00:05:32,332 --> 00:05:33,708
I want to sing better.

115
00:05:35,877 --> 00:05:38,796
Well, I'd like to teach you too,

116
00:05:39,505 --> 00:05:41,257
but something happened recently.

117
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:44,385
So I'm hesitant to teach.

118
00:05:44,469 --> 00:05:46,471
I'm sure Tarzzan sings better.

119
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:49,390
I've never sung properly.

120
00:05:49,474 --> 00:05:51,434
Sure, I've sung at karaoke,

121
00:05:51,517 --> 00:05:54,145
but I've never really sung properly.

122
00:05:54,228 --> 00:05:56,564
But I don't think I should teach anyone.

123
00:05:57,273 --> 00:06:00,276
Tarzzan, do you know what happened to him?

124
00:06:00,359 --> 00:06:01,736
No, I don't.

125
00:06:01,819 --> 00:06:03,404
Please. Please, don't watch it.

126
00:06:04,864 --> 00:06:06,616
-Just see me here.
-Hello.

127
00:06:06,699 --> 00:06:08,242
RIGHT THEN, SOMEONE ARRIVES

128
00:06:08,326 --> 00:06:09,869
-What was his name?
-Hello.

129
00:06:10,828 --> 00:06:12,413
-Just see me here.
-Hello.

130
00:06:13,331 --> 00:06:17,543
DOWOON

131
00:06:18,419 --> 00:06:20,129
ANOTHER UNEXPECTED MEMBER

132
00:06:20,213 --> 00:06:21,422
Dowoon of DAY6.

133
00:06:21,506 --> 00:06:23,466
-It's nice to meet you.
-Likewise.

134
00:06:23,549 --> 00:06:24,759
-Nice to meet you.
-Wow.

135
00:06:24,842 --> 00:06:27,637
Do you two know each other?

136
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:29,514
We just greeted each other once.

137
00:06:29,597 --> 00:06:31,182
-I know Young K.
-That's right.

138
00:06:31,265 --> 00:06:34,060
But Dowoon and I
have never met in private.

139
00:06:34,143 --> 00:06:36,104
What a spectacular lineup.

140
00:06:37,146 --> 00:06:38,314
You think so?

141
00:06:38,397 --> 00:06:39,273
Yes.

142
00:06:39,357 --> 00:06:41,400
I mean, I love being among them!

143
00:06:43,945 --> 00:06:45,988
Gosh, I watched your videos a lot.

144
00:06:48,241 --> 00:06:50,827
I'd only heard your voice before, but…

145
00:06:50,910 --> 00:06:52,036
-Did you watch me?
-Yes.

146
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:53,204
Really? Wow.

147
00:06:53,287 --> 00:06:54,330
THIS YOUNG MAN IS…

148
00:06:54,413 --> 00:06:57,083
DOWOON, THE DRUMMER OF DAY6

149
00:06:57,166 --> 00:06:58,709
DAY6'S YOUNGEST MEMBER

150
00:06:58,793 --> 00:07:00,378
DOWOON

151
00:07:01,796 --> 00:07:03,798
KNOWN FOR HAVING A LOT OF HOBBIES

152
00:07:04,841 --> 00:07:05,967
Can I ask where you're from?

153
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:08,511
-You're from Ulsan, right? I'm from Busan.
-Yes.

154
00:07:08,594 --> 00:07:10,012
I have an Ulsan accent.

155
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:11,556
Mine's a mix of Busan and Changwon.

156
00:07:11,639 --> 00:07:13,599
I also have Busan and Ulsan accents.

157
00:07:13,683 --> 00:07:14,809
-Really?
-Yes.

158
00:07:14,892 --> 00:07:17,103
-So you grew up in Ulsan?
-I did.

159
00:07:17,812 --> 00:07:19,772
So you grew up there and moved to Busan?

160
00:07:19,856 --> 00:07:22,400
I went to high school in Busan.

161
00:07:22,483 --> 00:07:23,651
BECOMING FRIENDS RIGHT AWAY

162
00:07:23,734 --> 00:07:24,944
-An arts high school?
-Yes.

163
00:07:25,027 --> 00:07:25,945
In Geumjeong-gu.

164
00:07:26,028 --> 00:07:28,030
FEELING AWKWARD SINCE HE'S FROM INCHEON

165
00:07:28,114 --> 00:07:30,408
-I went to Busan Arts School.
-We were really close.

166
00:07:31,617 --> 00:07:33,453
Busan Arts School was better.

167
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:36,122
-On the hill…
-His school was better?

168
00:07:38,166 --> 00:07:41,127
I went to a DAY6 concert,
and what I loved about him is…

169
00:07:41,210 --> 00:07:42,128
You did?

170
00:07:42,211 --> 00:07:44,464
Young K was like,

171
00:07:45,131 --> 00:07:48,259
"We've gone through so much
to come this far."

172
00:07:48,342 --> 00:07:50,636
He was emotional and thanking the fans.

173
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:52,263
Then he said, "This is nice!"

174
00:07:53,306 --> 00:07:55,391
I was like, "I love him!"

175
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:57,518
"He's so cool."

176
00:07:57,602 --> 00:07:59,103
IT'S ONE OF HIS CHARMS

177
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:00,021
It wasn't like that.

178
00:08:00,104 --> 00:08:02,690
I really loved his vibe.

179
00:08:02,773 --> 00:08:04,692
I like you a lot, too.

180
00:08:04,775 --> 00:08:06,152
On YouTube,

181
00:08:06,235 --> 00:08:10,364
I saw your videos,
and the titles were already so funny.

182
00:08:10,448 --> 00:08:11,616
What videos did you watch?

183
00:08:12,158 --> 00:08:13,284
SENSITIVE

184
00:08:13,367 --> 00:08:15,620
What, are you interrogating him?

185
00:08:15,703 --> 00:08:18,247
It's just that recently,
something happened, so…

186
00:08:18,331 --> 00:08:19,999
Because he might've watched that?

187
00:08:20,082 --> 00:08:22,543
The title was…
It was a video someone else filmed.

188
00:08:22,627 --> 00:08:25,421
I love all of your songs
and live performances.

189
00:08:25,505 --> 00:08:26,797
But their videos are like,

190
00:08:26,881 --> 00:08:29,008
"Car, the Garden's
terrible live performance."

191
00:08:29,091 --> 00:08:31,135
They're always titled that way.

192
00:08:31,219 --> 00:08:33,179
-But that was so…
-No, that's not it.

193
00:08:33,262 --> 00:08:35,556
"The live performance of 'Tree'
was a disaster."

194
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:36,641
Yes, that's it!

195
00:08:36,724 --> 00:08:39,060
But they also upload something
like "It wasn't bad today."

196
00:08:39,143 --> 00:08:40,937
HYPING HIM UP WHILE PUSHING HIM AWAY

197
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:42,313
He didn't want it brought up.

198
00:08:42,396 --> 00:08:43,397
HYPED UP AND SIDELINED

199
00:08:43,481 --> 00:08:44,899
-But…
-"A disaster."

200
00:08:44,982 --> 00:08:46,651
I think they're a true fan.

201
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:49,028
There was a dog…

202
00:08:49,111 --> 00:08:51,197
There was a dog emoticon.

203
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:52,281
Right.

204
00:08:52,365 --> 00:08:54,408
This is the first meeting.

205
00:08:54,492 --> 00:08:56,244
I'm so shy around strangers.

206
00:08:57,703 --> 00:09:01,541
NOW, THE LAST MEMBER ENTERS

207
00:09:01,624 --> 00:09:03,042
It's pure evil.

208
00:09:07,213 --> 00:09:08,464
-Hello.
-Hello.

209
00:09:08,548 --> 00:09:09,549
-Hello.
-Hello.

210
00:09:09,632 --> 00:09:10,466
Hello.

211
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:12,134
-Hello.
-He's a real actor.

212
00:09:12,218 --> 00:09:13,386
LEE CHAE-MIN

213
00:09:13,469 --> 00:09:15,846
FEELING AWKWARD

214
00:09:15,930 --> 00:09:17,056
-Hello.
-Wow.

215
00:09:17,139 --> 00:09:18,766
-It's unbelievable.
-I felt that way too.

216
00:09:18,849 --> 00:09:20,017
Unbelievable.

217
00:09:20,101 --> 00:09:21,060
Nice to meet you.

218
00:09:22,186 --> 00:09:24,939
ACTOR LEE CHAE-MIN

219
00:09:25,022 --> 00:09:28,359
UP-AND-COMING ACTOR WITH A HANDSOME FACE
AND A WIDE RANGE OF ACTING ABILITIES

220
00:09:29,527 --> 00:09:31,737
AFTER PLAYING LEE HEON
IN BON APPETIT, YOUR MAJESTY,

221
00:09:31,821 --> 00:09:35,408
HE'S BECOME A RISING STAR
WITH A LOT OF UPCOMING PROJECTS

222
00:09:36,158 --> 00:09:37,743
This is actor Lee Chae-min.

223
00:09:37,827 --> 00:09:39,161
Right. Hello.

224
00:09:39,245 --> 00:09:41,122
Hello. It's nice to meet you.

225
00:09:41,205 --> 00:09:42,665
Everyone's so handsome.

226
00:09:43,499 --> 00:09:44,959
THINKING OUT LOUD

227
00:09:45,042 --> 00:09:45,918
Right.

228
00:09:46,002 --> 00:09:47,545
You know his group, right?

229
00:09:47,628 --> 00:09:48,754
ALLDAY PROJECT.

230
00:09:49,422 --> 00:09:51,090
Like this.

231
00:09:51,757 --> 00:09:53,718
AS BEFITS A FORMER MC OF MUSIC BANK

232
00:09:53,801 --> 00:09:56,137
-And him?
-Of course, I know him.

233
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:58,014
Have you watched his recent video?

234
00:09:58,097 --> 00:09:59,765
You mean, the live performance?

235
00:10:01,475 --> 00:10:03,519
-What was it? Live…
-Everyone watched it.

236
00:10:03,603 --> 00:10:05,271
What was it?

237
00:10:05,354 --> 00:10:06,689
But I liked it.

238
00:10:06,772 --> 00:10:08,816
So did I. The title was so cute.

239
00:10:08,899 --> 00:10:09,984
"A disaster."

240
00:10:10,901 --> 00:10:14,071
So it's even spread
to the acting world like a disease.

241
00:10:14,155 --> 00:10:15,573
That video…

242
00:10:15,656 --> 00:10:18,367
No, I liked your live broadcast too.

243
00:10:18,451 --> 00:10:19,660
SKILL CONTROVERSY BROADCAST

244
00:10:19,744 --> 00:10:21,329
The one where he said how he felt?

245
00:10:21,412 --> 00:10:23,164
I thought it was cool.

246
00:10:23,247 --> 00:10:24,415
In what way?

247
00:10:24,498 --> 00:10:25,416
You know…

248
00:10:25,499 --> 00:10:26,626
GO ON, CHAE-MIN

249
00:10:26,709 --> 00:10:29,253
Well, something like that, I…

250
00:10:29,337 --> 00:10:30,713
You know, I just…

251
00:10:30,796 --> 00:10:32,632
NO REASON

252
00:10:32,715 --> 00:10:35,301
So it was a feeling
that's hard to describe.

253
00:10:35,384 --> 00:10:37,970
-I really love your song "Tree."
-Me too.

254
00:10:38,054 --> 00:10:39,221
Thank you.

255
00:10:40,473 --> 00:10:43,142
All right, so you four are the members.

256
00:10:45,436 --> 00:10:47,563
-It's nice to meet you.
-The pleasure is mine.

257
00:10:49,565 --> 00:10:53,444
We're gathered here today
so we can get to know each other.

258
00:10:53,527 --> 00:10:56,572
-And that's why we did the questionnaire.
-Right.

259
00:10:56,656 --> 00:10:58,407
LIFESTYLE, PHYSICAL ACTIVITY QUESTIONNAIRE

260
00:10:58,491 --> 00:11:00,284
IT WAS SENT TO THEM BEFORE FILMING

261
00:11:02,578 --> 00:11:04,455
ALL FOUR OF THEM COMPLETED IT

262
00:11:04,538 --> 00:11:07,083
All of you will be working together.

263
00:11:07,166 --> 00:11:09,251
I thought it'd be nice for you

264
00:11:09,335 --> 00:11:11,587
to get to know each other better today.

265
00:11:11,671 --> 00:11:14,298
So we'll reveal them to everyone here.

266
00:11:14,382 --> 00:11:16,050
Oh, it was meant to be revealed?

267
00:11:17,927 --> 00:11:19,303
CAR, THE GARDEN

268
00:11:19,387 --> 00:11:22,181
Car, the garden's strengths.

269
00:11:22,264 --> 00:11:24,475
Admits mistakes
and engages in self-reflection fast.

270
00:11:25,518 --> 00:11:26,477
I really do.

271
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:27,937
It reflects his recent activities.

272
00:11:28,646 --> 00:11:30,314
His weakness is that he's impatient.

273
00:11:31,148 --> 00:11:33,025
-You are?
-I'm so impatient.

274
00:11:33,109 --> 00:11:34,110
I even eat fast.

275
00:11:34,193 --> 00:11:36,195
So I don't like to be part of a group.

276
00:11:37,905 --> 00:11:39,865
Oh, no. He'll scold us a lot.

277
00:11:40,908 --> 00:11:41,784
He'll…

278
00:11:41,867 --> 00:11:43,411
Since I'm so impatient…

279
00:11:43,494 --> 00:11:45,579
So when you drive, do you use high beams?

280
00:11:46,831 --> 00:11:47,998
-I don't.
-No?

281
00:11:48,082 --> 00:11:49,417
I'm not like that.

282
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:50,876
-Like this.
-No.

283
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:52,628
I don't even know how to use them.

284
00:11:53,337 --> 00:11:54,422
High beams…

285
00:11:54,505 --> 00:11:57,091
In any case,
I think you're quite impatient.

286
00:11:57,174 --> 00:12:00,094
Your favorite dishes
are <i>mandu</i> and chicken dishes.

287
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:02,721
You're allergic to cucumbers?

288
00:12:03,472 --> 00:12:06,517
I'm not, but I wrote that
because you might make me eat them.

289
00:12:07,601 --> 00:12:10,604
I thought you wouldn't make me eat them
if I'm allergic.

290
00:12:10,688 --> 00:12:13,524
"What's the most recent book
you've read?" "None."

291
00:12:13,607 --> 00:12:15,359
I read some books of quotations.

292
00:12:16,026 --> 00:12:17,069
Through Reels.

293
00:12:17,153 --> 00:12:18,821
-Reels?
-Reels?

294
00:12:18,904 --> 00:12:20,656
AN UNEXPECTED WAY OF READING

295
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:23,742
-Reading them through Reels?
-Yes.

296
00:12:23,826 --> 00:12:25,870
Can you tell us some famous sayings?

297
00:12:25,953 --> 00:12:27,204
"Know yourself."

298
00:12:27,288 --> 00:12:28,164
Oh…

299
00:12:29,373 --> 00:12:30,875
You got that from Reels?

300
00:12:30,958 --> 00:12:32,918
EVEN HE FINDS IT RIDICULOUS

301
00:12:33,002 --> 00:12:34,253
-It's a good saying.
-Right.

302
00:12:34,336 --> 00:12:36,630
"If you regularly exercise
for your stamina,

303
00:12:36,714 --> 00:12:40,134
write in detail, such as
which exercise, how many times, etc."

304
00:12:40,217 --> 00:12:41,218
"None."

305
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:44,388
You must've finished it fast.

306
00:12:46,056 --> 00:12:47,558
It wasn't hard to answer.

307
00:12:48,559 --> 00:12:53,481
"On a scale of 1 to 100, how would you
grade your stamina? And why?"

308
00:12:54,148 --> 00:12:55,441
"Grade: 20 points."

309
00:12:56,192 --> 00:12:58,444
"Reason: I don't exercise
and am gaining weight."

310
00:13:00,404 --> 00:13:01,363
His character is…

311
00:13:01,447 --> 00:13:03,491
"I don't exercise and am gaining weight."

312
00:13:03,574 --> 00:13:04,992
HIS SAD STORY

313
00:13:05,075 --> 00:13:05,993
His character is…

314
00:13:06,076 --> 00:13:07,953
So he does know himself.

315
00:13:08,037 --> 00:13:09,330
I KNOW MYSELF

316
00:13:09,413 --> 00:13:11,832
-Let's see what kind of person Dowoon is.
-Right.

317
00:13:13,042 --> 00:13:15,044
He has a lot of hobbies.

318
00:13:15,127 --> 00:13:16,754
Gaming, fishing,

319
00:13:16,837 --> 00:13:18,464
-plant care.
-Oh, right.

320
00:13:18,547 --> 00:13:20,257
-Tending to plants.
-Plant care?

321
00:13:20,341 --> 00:13:22,801
Boxing, browsing used cars.

322
00:13:26,722 --> 00:13:27,932
Right, that's fun.

323
00:13:29,433 --> 00:13:31,101
I do this lately.

324
00:13:31,185 --> 00:13:32,937
Everyone dreams of certain cars.

325
00:13:33,020 --> 00:13:36,106
Like, "I think I can afford
a car like this." It's so fun.

326
00:13:37,233 --> 00:13:38,734
"Should I buy this or not?"

327
00:13:38,817 --> 00:13:39,944
Right, exactly.

328
00:13:40,027 --> 00:13:42,196
-Imagining.
-Right.

329
00:13:42,279 --> 00:13:45,241
"What is your favorite movie
or drama show?"

330
00:13:45,324 --> 00:13:48,410
The answer is
"The Dream Life of Kim Living in Seoul."

331
00:13:49,036 --> 00:13:51,080
-Seriously. It's a masterpiece.
-Sorry,

332
00:13:51,163 --> 00:13:54,375
but the correct title is
<i>The Dream Life of Mr. Kim.</i>

333
00:13:54,458 --> 00:13:57,086
"The Dream Life of Kim Living in Seoul."

334
00:13:58,587 --> 00:14:00,548
HE DOESN'T KNOW
THE TITLE OF HIS FAVORITE DRAMA

335
00:14:00,631 --> 00:14:01,882
Who is this Kim?

336
00:14:01,966 --> 00:14:03,217
Is he your neighbor?

337
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:04,969
I wrote it without looking it up.

338
00:14:05,052 --> 00:14:06,804
"The Dream Life of Kim Living in Seoul."

339
00:14:06,887 --> 00:14:08,722
And "Howl's Castle."

340
00:14:08,806 --> 00:14:10,099
<i>Howl's Moving Castle.</i>

341
00:14:10,182 --> 00:14:11,767
It's "Howl's Moving Castle."

342
00:14:12,977 --> 00:14:14,395
NO WONDER IT FELT SHORT

343
00:14:14,478 --> 00:14:16,522
But seriously, I love them.

344
00:14:16,605 --> 00:14:18,440
Yet you wrote the wrong titles.

345
00:14:18,524 --> 00:14:20,651
I think he and I have a lot in common.

346
00:14:20,734 --> 00:14:22,027
Yes, I think so.

347
00:14:22,111 --> 00:14:25,030
We're not so detailed,
but once we start something…

348
00:14:25,114 --> 00:14:27,575
You put it in such a great way.

349
00:14:29,410 --> 00:14:31,787
"Practice kickboxing
three to four times a week."

350
00:14:31,871 --> 00:14:33,622
"Sparring, shadowboxing."

351
00:14:33,706 --> 00:14:34,665
"Kicking."

352
00:14:37,209 --> 00:14:38,919
Who says that?

353
00:14:39,003 --> 00:14:40,921
Who says kicking as a hobby?

354
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:41,922
Because…

355
00:14:42,006 --> 00:14:43,257
Maybe "practice kicking."

356
00:14:43,340 --> 00:14:44,884
RIGHT, IT'S KICKBOXING

357
00:14:44,967 --> 00:14:47,970
In the beginning, it sounds good.
"Sparring, shadowboxing."

358
00:14:48,053 --> 00:14:49,430
Then, "kicking."

359
00:14:49,513 --> 00:14:51,515
You're right. It sounds awkward.

360
00:14:51,599 --> 00:14:52,433
That was it.

361
00:14:52,516 --> 00:14:55,227
"Which of the following
physical activities do you prefer?"

362
00:14:55,311 --> 00:14:56,145
"Hiking."

363
00:14:56,228 --> 00:14:58,105
Right, I think hiking is really good.

364
00:14:58,188 --> 00:15:00,482
-Have you done it before?
-Sure, I have.

365
00:15:00,566 --> 00:15:03,068
When you reach the top,
you feel so refreshed.

366
00:15:03,819 --> 00:15:07,406
And it feels so cool on the top
in the summer.

367
00:15:07,489 --> 00:15:11,243
"On a scale of 1 to 100,
how would you grade your stamina?"

368
00:15:11,327 --> 00:15:12,578
"Eighty points."

369
00:15:12,661 --> 00:15:15,706
"I haven't exercised in two years,
but my stamina is much better."

370
00:15:15,789 --> 00:15:17,416
What does this mean?

371
00:15:20,127 --> 00:15:21,295
I know what he means.

372
00:15:22,296 --> 00:15:23,589
Do you?

373
00:15:23,672 --> 00:15:25,049
He can translate it.

374
00:15:25,132 --> 00:15:26,008
Translate it for us.

375
00:15:26,091 --> 00:15:30,429
-So, he used to work out regularly.
-Okay.

376
00:15:30,512 --> 00:15:33,974
But he hadn't for two years,
so he thought his stamina would be worse.

377
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:36,101
But it turns out it's still good.

378
00:15:36,185 --> 00:15:37,227
That's right.

379
00:15:37,311 --> 00:15:38,228
AMAZING TRANSLATION

380
00:15:38,312 --> 00:15:40,272
-Is it accurate?
-Yes, it is.

381
00:15:40,356 --> 00:15:41,857
I used to work out at the gym.

382
00:15:42,566 --> 00:15:43,984
Then I stopped for two years.

383
00:15:44,068 --> 00:15:45,069
THE TWO ARE LIKEMINDED

384
00:15:45,152 --> 00:15:46,362
Next is Chae-min.

385
00:15:46,445 --> 00:15:47,738
LEE CHAE-MIN

386
00:15:47,821 --> 00:15:49,657
"What are your hobbies?"

387
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:52,785
"Basketball, piano,
learning guitar lately?"

388
00:15:54,578 --> 00:15:55,996
Then are you a member of a club?

389
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:56,997
Yes.

390
00:15:57,623 --> 00:15:58,874
You're doing it properly.

391
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:00,250
You also do streetball.

392
00:16:00,334 --> 00:16:01,919
-I love basketball too.
-Really?

393
00:16:02,503 --> 00:16:04,672
I think I've seen you play.

394
00:16:04,755 --> 00:16:06,048
-Really?
-Maybe not?

395
00:16:06,131 --> 00:16:06,966
On the street?

396
00:16:07,049 --> 00:16:08,217
While passing by?

397
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:09,468
Honestly, I just said that.

398
00:16:10,594 --> 00:16:11,595
I'm sorry.

399
00:16:11,679 --> 00:16:13,013
At a park in Hangang River?

400
00:16:13,097 --> 00:16:16,016
Yes, and I also play at Banpo Stadium.

401
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:17,309
Do you live in Banpo?

402
00:16:17,393 --> 00:16:18,560
No, in Cheongdam.

403
00:16:20,521 --> 00:16:22,147
No, no.

404
00:16:22,231 --> 00:16:24,358
Why were you suddenly curious about that?

405
00:16:25,150 --> 00:16:27,861
You see, we shouldn't be like this.

406
00:16:27,945 --> 00:16:30,447
I lied to him just now
without realizing it.

407
00:16:30,531 --> 00:16:31,949
I said I probably saw him.

408
00:16:32,032 --> 00:16:32,866
It was a lie.

409
00:16:32,950 --> 00:16:36,286
We should stop this
to really get close to each other.

410
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:39,915
"If you have any habit or method
for your stamina…"

411
00:16:39,999 --> 00:16:40,874
"Juice."

412
00:16:40,958 --> 00:16:43,794
-He wrote "Juice."
-Juice?

413
00:16:43,877 --> 00:16:44,712
What kind of juice?

414
00:16:44,795 --> 00:16:47,464
I drink thistle juice,
which is good for the liver.

415
00:16:48,173 --> 00:16:51,218
And cabbage juice,
which is good for the stomach.

416
00:16:51,301 --> 00:16:52,386
I have it every morning.

417
00:16:52,469 --> 00:16:55,139
You parents help you with it?
Like the supplements?

418
00:16:55,222 --> 00:16:56,390
Or by yourself?

419
00:16:56,473 --> 00:16:58,642
-I live alone right now.
-So by yourself?

420
00:16:58,726 --> 00:17:00,978
-So by myself.
-You live alone in Cheongdam?

421
00:17:03,147 --> 00:17:04,481
That's amazing.

422
00:17:04,565 --> 00:17:05,524
No…

423
00:17:05,607 --> 00:17:07,109
You're still on that?

424
00:17:07,192 --> 00:17:08,027
He's intimidated.

425
00:17:08,944 --> 00:17:10,237
I am intimidated.

426
00:17:10,320 --> 00:17:12,531
No, it's not that kind of house.

427
00:17:13,282 --> 00:17:14,783
What you hate the most is hiking.

428
00:17:15,492 --> 00:17:16,910
Why do you hate hiking?

429
00:17:16,994 --> 00:17:19,663
I don't really hate it.
I just haven't done it much,

430
00:17:19,747 --> 00:17:22,624
so I don't know
the beauty of it yet, I think.

431
00:17:23,417 --> 00:17:25,085
So you don't do cardio much?

432
00:17:25,169 --> 00:17:28,797
I don't really like running.
I just like competitive sports.

433
00:17:28,881 --> 00:17:30,215
So I play basketball.

434
00:17:30,299 --> 00:17:32,259
If I have to run, it has to be a race.

435
00:17:32,342 --> 00:17:33,385
Competitive.

436
00:17:33,469 --> 00:17:34,720
Yes, I'm quite competitive.

437
00:17:35,679 --> 00:17:37,765
So you have to crush others.

438
00:17:37,848 --> 00:17:39,266
"Crush others."

439
00:17:39,349 --> 00:17:40,893
You enjoy crushing others.

440
00:17:40,976 --> 00:17:42,644
"Crush others."

441
00:17:42,728 --> 00:17:45,731
On a scale of 1 to 100,
you graded your stamina a 70.

442
00:17:45,814 --> 00:17:47,858
-The reason is…
-It's lower than expected.

443
00:17:47,941 --> 00:17:50,444
Right. You work out every day
and play basketball. Why?

444
00:17:50,527 --> 00:17:52,112
Since I work out every day,

445
00:17:52,196 --> 00:17:53,822
I feel tired all the time.

446
00:17:53,906 --> 00:17:56,658
So all the working out
makes your stamina worse?

447
00:17:56,742 --> 00:18:00,287
I think so, but you know, I think…

448
00:18:00,370 --> 00:18:02,164
I enjoy making myself exhausted.

449
00:18:02,998 --> 00:18:05,667
I can't stand just relaxing and resting.

450
00:18:06,335 --> 00:18:08,253
I only relax and rest when I sleep.

451
00:18:09,588 --> 00:18:11,173
You'll definitely make it big…

452
00:18:11,256 --> 00:18:13,926
You're already successful,
but you'll become a superstar.

453
00:18:14,009 --> 00:18:15,344
"Superstar."

454
00:18:15,427 --> 00:18:17,429
-You have the feeling?
-Yes, I do.

455
00:18:17,513 --> 00:18:18,639
In what way?

456
00:18:18,722 --> 00:18:21,642
If I were him, I'd be so completed.

457
00:18:21,725 --> 00:18:22,684
What?

458
00:18:22,768 --> 00:18:24,561
I mean, complacent.

459
00:18:27,648 --> 00:18:28,774
"So complacent."

460
00:18:28,857 --> 00:18:30,025
I heard it wrong.

461
00:18:31,151 --> 00:18:32,778
So that's why everyone was silent.

462
00:18:33,612 --> 00:18:35,322
-All right.
-So lastly,

463
00:18:35,405 --> 00:18:36,615
-the youngest one, then?
-Yes.

464
00:18:36,698 --> 00:18:37,533
TARZZAN

465
00:18:37,616 --> 00:18:39,743
-I'm curious about him the most.
-Me too.

466
00:18:39,827 --> 00:18:42,246
"Usually, I go to bed
around 3 to 4:00 a.m.

467
00:18:42,329 --> 00:18:43,831
and wake up around 1:00 p.m.

468
00:18:44,790 --> 00:18:45,624
SIMILAR HABITS

469
00:18:45,707 --> 00:18:47,251
I knew it. Country folks are alike.

470
00:18:47,334 --> 00:18:48,585
"Country folks."

471
00:18:48,669 --> 00:18:50,671
What does that have to do with this?

472
00:18:50,754 --> 00:18:55,342
My schedule is so tight,
it feels like a day is 48 hours.

473
00:18:55,425 --> 00:18:57,803
So I tend to sleep for a long time.

474
00:18:57,886 --> 00:19:02,015
"What do you think
your strengths and weaknesses are?"

475
00:19:02,099 --> 00:19:03,976
"I'm honest and extreme."

476
00:19:04,768 --> 00:19:06,645
Meaning, "All in or all out."

477
00:19:06,728 --> 00:19:08,897
He's a star.
Those are the traits of a star.

478
00:19:08,981 --> 00:19:10,524
Star? Is that a thing?

479
00:19:10,607 --> 00:19:11,900
TWO RISING STARS

480
00:19:11,984 --> 00:19:12,901
The traits of stars?

481
00:19:12,985 --> 00:19:16,196
His favorite movie shows that too.

482
00:19:16,280 --> 00:19:17,281
<i>A Star is Born.</i>

483
00:19:18,031 --> 00:19:18,907
Me too.

484
00:19:18,991 --> 00:19:20,200
That's my favorite too.

485
00:19:20,284 --> 00:19:22,619
The activity he prefers the most.

486
00:19:22,703 --> 00:19:24,037
He picked swimming.

487
00:19:24,621 --> 00:19:27,499
In the lower grades of elementary school,

488
00:19:27,583 --> 00:19:29,209
I was a triathlete.

489
00:19:29,293 --> 00:19:30,544
Really?

490
00:19:30,627 --> 00:19:32,546
He's the real deal.

491
00:19:32,629 --> 00:19:34,840
SINCE MIDDLE SCHOOL,
HE WON MODERN DANCE COMPETITIONS

492
00:19:34,923 --> 00:19:37,259
The gap between him and the others
are widening.

493
00:19:37,342 --> 00:19:39,303
I like it because…

494
00:19:39,887 --> 00:19:42,139
he can come to the rescue
when I'm in trouble.

495
00:19:42,890 --> 00:19:44,057
-When in trouble?
-Yes.

496
00:19:44,141 --> 00:19:48,270
"On a scale of 1 to 100,
how would you grade your stamina?"

497
00:19:48,854 --> 00:19:50,647
He wrote 60.

498
00:19:51,273 --> 00:19:52,816
You two are fitter than us, though.

499
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:56,320
"My physical abilities are definitely
not as good as the old days."

500
00:19:56,403 --> 00:19:58,238
On a scale of 1 to 100,

501
00:19:58,322 --> 00:20:02,618
compared to when I used to work out a lot,
my physical abilities are much weaker.

502
00:20:02,701 --> 00:20:03,994
You know yourself best.

503
00:20:04,077 --> 00:20:04,912
Right.

504
00:20:04,995 --> 00:20:06,622
You're so upright, both of you.

505
00:20:08,916 --> 00:20:09,875
"Upright."

506
00:20:11,793 --> 00:20:14,922
All right.
Since it's our first meeting today,

507
00:20:15,005 --> 00:20:18,759
we tried to get to know each other
better through this.

508
00:20:18,842 --> 00:20:21,803
What's most important is actually
what we'll do together.

509
00:20:22,679 --> 00:20:24,640
-I'm so curious.
-So am I.

510
00:20:24,723 --> 00:20:26,141
That's what's important.

511
00:20:26,225 --> 00:20:28,060
All of you have something in common.

512
00:20:28,143 --> 00:20:29,269
We can't lie.

513
00:20:29,895 --> 00:20:31,438
-We're honest.
-Honesty.

514
00:20:31,521 --> 00:20:33,565
Well, what I have in common with them is…

515
00:20:33,649 --> 00:20:35,484
-I'm a man.
-We're men.

516
00:20:35,567 --> 00:20:37,027
And we're Korean.

517
00:20:37,110 --> 00:20:39,112
HE ONLY SPEAKS FACTS

518
00:20:39,196 --> 00:20:40,489
Well, we thought

519
00:20:40,572 --> 00:20:42,699
what you have in common

520
