CLIMBED SEORAKSAN MORE THAN 300 TIMES

660
00:26:48,356 --> 00:26:49,357
CHAPTER 1
WHAT IS HIKING?

661
00:26:49,441 --> 00:26:50,900
When we hike a mountain,

662
00:26:50,984 --> 00:26:54,446
we usually spend roughly 40%
of our energy going up,

663
00:26:54,529 --> 00:26:55,697
30% coming down,

664
00:26:55,780 --> 00:26:58,033
and save the remaining 30% just in case.

665
00:26:58,116 --> 00:27:00,035
ASCENT 40 : DESCENT 30 : RESERVE 30

666
00:27:00,118 --> 00:27:02,746
While hiking, you get hungry, right?

667
00:27:02,829 --> 00:27:04,581
If your energy is low, what do you do?

668
00:27:04,664 --> 00:27:05,749
-You eat.
-You eat.

669
00:27:05,832 --> 00:27:08,168
It's better to eat before you feel hungry.

670
00:27:08,251 --> 00:27:10,628
Your favorite treats,
snacks, and trail food.

671
00:27:11,671 --> 00:27:15,258
Something you can snack on often,
even if it's low in calories.

672
00:27:15,342 --> 00:27:16,176
How about <i>mandu?</i>

673
00:27:16,259 --> 00:27:18,178
That's not good. Why?

674
00:27:18,261 --> 00:27:20,263
It should be easy to carry.

675
00:27:20,347 --> 00:27:22,891
Something you can eat while you're moving.

676
00:27:22,974 --> 00:27:24,517
-Like energy bars.
-Exactly.

677
00:27:24,601 --> 00:27:26,061
Oh, energy bars.

678
00:27:26,144 --> 00:27:28,521
And you can choose what you prefer.

679
00:27:28,605 --> 00:27:30,774
Then it'll produce energy right away.

680
00:27:31,566 --> 00:27:33,485
And you'll spend it while moving, right?

681
00:27:33,568 --> 00:27:34,778
-Yes.
-How about saving?

682
00:27:35,362 --> 00:27:36,363
-Saving?
-Saving?

683
00:27:36,446 --> 00:27:39,282
The layering system.

684
00:27:39,366 --> 00:27:40,533
-Layering?
-Yes.

685
00:27:40,617 --> 00:27:43,453
To put it simply,
wearing several layers of clothing.

686
00:27:43,536 --> 00:27:44,996
How? Well.

687
00:27:45,080 --> 00:27:46,998
You should do it well.

688
00:27:47,082 --> 00:27:50,126
If you do it carelessly,
it won't be very efficient.

689
00:27:50,210 --> 00:27:51,544
So you must do it well.

690
00:27:51,628 --> 00:27:53,797
CHAPTER 2
THE LAYERING SYSTEM

691
00:27:53,880 --> 00:27:56,883
<i>The layering system</i>
<i>consists of three layers.</i>

692
00:27:56,966 --> 00:27:57,842
<i>First,</i>

693
00:27:58,802 --> 00:28:01,179
<i>the Base Layer for wicking sweat away.</i>

694
00:28:01,805 --> 00:28:05,975
<i>It is recommended to wear moisture-wicking</i>
<i>and quick-drying clothes</i>

695
00:28:06,059 --> 00:28:08,603
<i>to prevent a drop in body temperature.</i>

696
00:28:09,270 --> 00:28:10,230
<i>Second,</i>

697
00:28:10,939 --> 00:28:13,650
<i>the Mid-Layer for insulation.</i>

698
00:28:14,526 --> 00:28:17,070
<i>A fleece is recommended,</i>

699
00:28:17,153 --> 00:28:20,073
<i>but you can also add</i>
<i>a lightweight down jacket if needed.</i>

700
00:28:20,740 --> 00:28:21,699
<i>Third,</i>

701
00:28:22,450 --> 00:28:25,954
<i>the Outer Layer,</i>
<i>a waterproof and windproof layer.</i>

702
00:28:27,038 --> 00:28:29,374
<i>On snowy or stormy days,</i>

703
00:28:29,457 --> 00:28:31,167
<i>it must be worn.</i>

704
00:28:32,502 --> 00:28:35,630
<i>We have gone over the layering system</i>
<i>for winter hiking.</i>

705
00:28:37,048 --> 00:28:39,759
<i>I hope you also make sure</i>
<i>you're properly equipped</i>

706
00:28:39,843 --> 00:28:41,803
<i>before hiking in winter.</i>

707
00:28:41,886 --> 00:28:43,763
PREPARE FOR A SAFE WINTER HIKE WITH GEAR

