777
00:30:59,732 --> 00:31:01,067
It's dangerous to follow them.

778
00:31:01,150 --> 00:31:02,277
STILL IN DOUBT

779
00:31:02,360 --> 00:31:05,947
It's better to move away
without showing your back.

780
00:31:06,030 --> 00:31:08,116
-Then they usually just go away?
-Yes.

781
00:31:08,908 --> 00:31:10,201
-Stay indifferent.
-Yes.

782
00:31:10,285 --> 00:31:11,286
I can do that.

783
00:31:11,369 --> 00:31:12,287
HE'S GOOD AT THAT

784
00:31:12,370 --> 00:31:13,288
You should do that.

785
00:31:13,872 --> 00:31:17,917
What kind of dangerous animals
have you come across while hiking?

786
00:31:19,419 --> 00:31:20,378
A snake.

787
00:31:21,921 --> 00:31:22,755
A snake.

788
00:31:22,839 --> 00:31:24,507
LESS DANGEROUS THAN EXPECTED

789
00:31:25,174 --> 00:31:27,594
It's quite common to run into wild boars.

790
00:31:28,428 --> 00:31:30,263
We've run into a snake before too.

791
00:31:30,346 --> 00:31:32,181
We should ignore snakes too?

792
00:31:32,265 --> 00:31:33,808
Yes, just pretend not to see them.

793
00:31:34,559 --> 00:31:37,478
-And just go around it.
-But it's hard to ignore snakes.

794
00:31:37,562 --> 00:31:39,355
Because if we lock eyes…

795
00:31:39,439 --> 00:31:41,983
-You were born in the Year of the Snake?
-I can't be sure.

796
00:31:42,066 --> 00:31:43,401
-No, the Horse.
-Oh, really?

797
00:31:44,861 --> 00:31:45,904
Anyway…

798
00:31:46,446 --> 00:31:48,114
But why did you think that?

799
00:31:50,116 --> 00:31:53,161
So if you see any wild animals,

800
00:31:53,244 --> 00:31:55,079
-just… Yes.
-Pretend not to see them.

801
00:31:55,163 --> 00:31:56,372
If you don't provoke them,

802
00:31:56,456 --> 00:31:57,999
DON'T FORGET TO IGNORE THEM

803
00:31:58,082 --> 00:32:00,335
-it won't be dangerous.
-Okay.

804
00:32:00,418 --> 00:32:02,712
-We won't know until we're up there.
-Right.

805
00:32:03,296 --> 00:32:06,424
It's better to try it once
than to hear about it a hundred times.

806
00:32:06,507 --> 00:32:09,093
Today, or when you have time,

807
00:32:09,177 --> 00:32:11,387
if you go hiking nearby, it'll be helpful.

808
00:32:11,471 --> 00:32:13,348
Right. I should go.

809
00:32:13,431 --> 00:32:15,016
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

810
00:32:15,099 --> 00:32:17,060
HIKING 101 ENDS

811
00:32:17,143 --> 00:32:19,228
WE PREPARED IT RIGHT AWAY

812
00:32:19,312 --> 00:32:20,229
MEMBERSHIP APPLICATION

813
00:32:22,857 --> 00:32:25,109
HIKING CLUB APPLICATION FORM
TO KEEP THEM FROM LEAVING

814
00:32:25,735 --> 00:32:30,949
THEY FILL IT IN WITHOUT COMPLAINING

815
00:32:31,699 --> 00:32:33,660
"Resolution: Give it your all."
You've changed.

816
00:32:33,743 --> 00:32:34,577
Yes.

817
00:32:36,120 --> 00:32:38,331
But my motto is
"Give up if it's too hard."

818
00:32:40,667 --> 00:32:42,877
Have you checked the club rules, everyone?

819
00:32:43,628 --> 00:32:46,339
Like, "Food is provided
if you complete the hike."

820
00:32:47,882 --> 00:32:49,759
I signed before I read it, darn it.

821
00:32:49,842 --> 00:32:53,096
If you give up halfway,
there will be no food.

822
00:32:54,138 --> 00:32:56,808
Why don't you choose the club president?

823
00:32:56,891 --> 00:32:59,477
Right. We'll take recommendations.

824
00:32:59,560 --> 00:33:00,520
I recommend Tarzzan.

825
00:33:00,603 --> 00:33:02,230
-What?
-One for Tarzzan.

826
00:33:02,313 --> 00:33:04,607
-And Dowoon?
-You should go with the flow.

827
00:33:04,691 --> 00:33:06,234
I recommend Tarzzan too.

828
00:33:06,317 --> 00:33:07,151
Okay, Tarzzan.

829
00:33:07,235 --> 00:33:08,611
Then same for me too.

830
00:33:08,695 --> 00:33:09,570
What…

831
00:33:09,654 --> 00:33:10,863
What about you, Tarzzan?

832
00:33:10,947 --> 00:33:12,490
Tarzzan's shining eyes.

833
00:33:12,573 --> 00:33:14,075
-Of course, I…
-His physical fitness.

834
00:33:14,951 --> 00:33:17,829
And while working with ALLDAY PROJECT,

835
00:33:17,912 --> 00:33:19,789
his mindset has become more suited

836
00:33:19,872 --> 00:33:21,040
to group activities.

837
00:33:22,125 --> 00:33:24,002
There's something you should know.

838
00:33:24,836 --> 00:33:28,214
The president can appoint the manager.

839
00:33:30,049 --> 00:33:31,592
-Hey…
-The manager is lower, right?

840
00:33:31,676 --> 00:33:32,844
Of course.

841
00:33:32,927 --> 00:33:34,220
I like it!

842
00:33:35,847 --> 00:33:36,806
President Tar.

843
00:33:37,682 --> 00:33:38,850
-Manager Car?
-Manager Car.

844
00:33:38,933 --> 00:33:39,767
It's him?

845
00:33:40,268 --> 00:33:41,853
Let's seal it with a round of applause.

846
00:33:45,732 --> 00:33:47,150
But you know what?

847
00:33:47,233 --> 00:33:50,028
The manager manages money.

848
00:33:50,111 --> 00:33:52,321
If we collect a membership fee,

849
00:33:52,405 --> 00:33:54,032
when we eat, you'll…

850
00:33:54,115 --> 00:33:55,575
I might pocket a little.

851
00:33:56,117 --> 00:33:57,368
You should let it slide.

852
00:33:57,452 --> 00:33:58,369
That's embezzlement.

853
00:33:58,453 --> 00:34:00,830
I'll treat you well, so please…

854
00:34:00,913 --> 00:34:02,248
All right.

855
00:34:02,331 --> 00:34:03,791
I'm the president, you know.

856
00:34:03,875 --> 00:34:05,918
PRESIDENT TAR

857
00:34:10,089 --> 00:34:13,092
PRESIDENT TAR WITH ANIMALISTIC ENERGY

858
00:34:13,176 --> 00:34:14,552
Let's go.

859
00:34:14,635 --> 00:34:16,804
We're almost there. Hang in there.

860
00:34:16,888 --> 00:34:18,014
Almost there.

861
00:34:18,097 --> 00:34:19,182
CHEERING THEM UP

862
00:34:20,058 --> 00:34:20,933
What did you write?

863
00:34:21,017 --> 00:34:22,268
"Why are we doing this?"

864
00:34:22,351 --> 00:34:23,978
BUT NOT VERY INTERESTED IN HIKING

865
00:34:24,062 --> 00:34:24,979
WHY ARE WE DOING THIS?

866
00:34:25,646 --> 00:34:28,941
The president started to plan himself.

867
00:34:29,025 --> 00:34:30,568
I did.

868
00:34:30,651 --> 00:34:33,362
EXCELLENT CHOICES OF RESTAURANTS

869
00:34:33,446 --> 00:34:34,280
SATISFIED

870
00:34:34,363 --> 00:34:36,157
-This is so good.
-Good discovery.

871
00:34:37,283 --> 00:34:38,493
Tarzzan found this place?

872
00:34:38,576 --> 00:34:40,328
-Yes, I did.
-It's so good.

873
00:34:40,411 --> 00:34:41,454
Nice discovery.

874
00:34:41,537 --> 00:34:42,997
I might throw up the abalone!

875
00:34:43,081 --> 00:34:45,374
THE PERFECT PLAN EVEN HE'S SATISFIED WITH

876
00:34:45,458 --> 00:34:47,752
I'm sure we'll go
to Ulsan, my hometown, too.

877
00:34:47,835 --> 00:34:48,878
It smells so good.

878
00:34:48,961 --> 00:34:50,379
THEN THEY ARRIVE

879
00:34:50,463 --> 00:34:53,549
AT HIS PARENTS' HOUSE
WHERE A FULL-COURSE MEAL IS SERVED

880
00:34:53,633 --> 00:34:54,592
Let's go!

881
00:34:54,675 --> 00:34:56,928
A MAN-OF-ACTION PRESIDENT
ONLY INTERESTED IN FOOD

882
00:34:58,054 --> 00:34:59,388
I dare you to go.

883
00:34:59,472 --> 00:35:01,390
AND HE IS IN DIFFERENT SPIRITS

884
00:35:01,474 --> 00:35:02,767
It's 32,500 won.

885
00:35:03,559 --> 00:35:04,769
Hey, let's…

886
00:35:04,852 --> 00:35:05,812
Where did they go?

887
00:35:05,895 --> 00:35:07,188
MANAGER CAR

888
00:35:07,271 --> 00:35:08,147
Where are they?

889
00:35:08,231 --> 00:35:09,982
Four bottles of water, please.

890
00:35:10,066 --> 00:35:11,150
PAYING IS ALWAYS HIS JOB

891
00:35:11,234 --> 00:35:12,485
Thank you for the drinks.

892
00:35:12,568 --> 00:35:13,611
I'll pay in cash.

893
00:35:13,694 --> 00:35:15,446
-Thanks.
-Thanks.

894
00:35:15,530 --> 00:35:16,864
We have to pay 12,000 won.

895
00:35:16,948 --> 00:35:18,491
All right, I'll pay.

896
00:35:18,574 --> 00:35:20,118
Never thought I'd ride a tandem bike.

897
00:35:20,201 --> 00:35:21,035
PAYING IS EASY

898
00:35:21,828 --> 00:35:23,121
SIGHING

899
00:35:23,204 --> 00:35:27,458
BUT HIKING IS SO HARD

900
00:35:27,542 --> 00:35:29,794
Seriously, this is so crappy.

901
00:35:29,877 --> 00:35:31,212
I hate it.

902
00:35:32,088 --> 00:35:33,589
The mountain's so annoying.

903
00:35:33,673 --> 00:35:35,591
I want to throw away these sticks.

904
00:35:35,675 --> 00:35:38,010
HE SAYS SOMETHING MEAN EVERY TIME HE HIKES

905
00:35:38,094 --> 00:35:39,804
For every negative comment, 100,000 won.

906
00:35:39,887 --> 00:35:41,139
Raise the fine.

907
00:35:41,222 --> 00:35:42,515
-Make it 300,000 won.
-Good.

908
00:35:42,598 --> 00:35:44,225
HE WAS CONFIDENT

909
00:35:44,308 --> 00:35:46,978
I don't think
I can do this program, seriously.

910
00:35:47,061 --> 00:35:48,646
-Wow.
-The fine.

911
00:35:48,729 --> 00:35:49,981
I'm sick of this.

912
00:35:50,690 --> 00:35:52,108
I'm fed up with it.

913
00:35:53,359 --> 00:35:55,486
-Hey.
-Why go up just to come down?

914
00:35:55,570 --> 00:35:56,863
Thanks for the fine.

915
00:35:58,906 --> 00:36:01,200
HE'S ABOUT TO GO BROKE

916
00:36:01,284 --> 00:36:02,952
<i>I'll pay 300,000 won.</i>

917
00:36:03,035 --> 00:36:05,246
THANKS TO HIM,
THEY HAVE MORE THAN ENOUGH MONEY

918
00:36:05,329 --> 00:36:08,207
You know Producer Nah, right?
Please report him to the police.

919
00:36:08,291 --> 00:36:09,959
HIS FINES ARE FEEDING THE MEMBERS

920
00:36:10,042 --> 00:36:11,085
Now…

921
00:36:11,169 --> 00:36:12,503
What are our positions?

922
00:36:13,129 --> 00:36:15,423
For Dowoon, how about
the Minister of Transport?

923
00:36:15,506 --> 00:36:17,341
MINISTER OF TRANSPORT

924
00:36:17,425 --> 00:36:18,467
Here we go.

925
00:36:18,551 --> 00:36:21,262
HE'S SATISFIED WITH HIS POSITION

926
00:36:21,345 --> 00:36:22,972
Let me know if it gets too hard.

927
00:36:23,055 --> 00:36:23,890
I'll be okay.

928
00:36:23,973 --> 00:36:25,933
I'm not that considerate.

929
00:36:26,017 --> 00:36:27,435
HOWEVER

930
00:36:27,518 --> 00:36:28,895
I'll tell you if I'm tired.

931
00:36:28,978 --> 00:36:31,606
I can just drive and pick them up, right?

932
00:36:31,689 --> 00:36:32,648
-Yes.
-Right?

933
00:36:33,441 --> 00:36:34,609
I'm here!

934
00:36:34,692 --> 00:36:38,446
VOLUNTARILY PICKING THEM UP

935
00:36:38,529 --> 00:36:40,031
Have this if you want.

936
00:36:40,698 --> 00:36:41,657
What do you want?

937
00:36:42,241 --> 00:36:43,367
I'll have the Cocoball Bar.

938
00:36:43,451 --> 00:36:45,077
TAKING CARE OF REFUELING TOO

939
00:36:45,161 --> 00:36:46,662
-Here, wear this.
-Okay.

940
00:36:48,372 --> 00:36:50,374
I earned a lot of brownie points.

941
00:36:50,458 --> 00:36:52,919
You're part of ALLDAY PROJECT now.

942
00:36:53,502 --> 00:36:55,171
Let me know if you need food.

943
00:36:55,254 --> 00:36:57,131
HE SEEMS TO ALWAYS SAY THE RIGHT THINGS

944
00:36:57,215 --> 00:36:59,008
I also have candy.

945
00:36:59,091 --> 00:37:01,427
Hey, do you know the Ulsan Alps?

946
00:37:01,510 --> 00:37:03,387
HE'S OFF COURSE

947
00:37:03,471 --> 00:37:05,806
No, the Yeongnam Alps.

948
00:37:05,890 --> 00:37:08,184
HE OFTEN GETS LOST WHILE TALKING

949
00:37:08,267 --> 00:37:11,020
For a second,
I thought there was carbonara in it.

950
00:37:11,103 --> 00:37:12,188
Wait, what was it?

951
00:37:12,271 --> 00:37:14,690
<i>Kkanari</i> something. Darn it.

952
00:37:14,774 --> 00:37:15,942
OFF COURSE AGAIN

953
00:37:16,025 --> 00:37:18,027
Lee Gwang-gyu is from my school too.

954
00:37:18,110 --> 00:37:19,779
-Kim Gwang-gyu?
-Right. Kim Gwang-gyu.

955
00:37:19,862 --> 00:37:21,405
OFF COURSE AGAIN

956
00:37:22,823 --> 00:37:25,660
HE'S BETTER SUITED FOR DRIVING, AFTER ALL

957
00:37:25,743 --> 00:37:26,827
<i>I'm exhausted.</i>

958
00:37:28,162 --> 00:37:30,623
AND THE LAST MEMBER

959
00:37:30,706 --> 00:37:32,375
<i>As the Minister of Foreign Affairs,</i>

960
00:37:33,084 --> 00:37:33,960
<i>my job is</i>

961
00:37:34,043 --> 00:37:37,338
to prevent any conflict between the staff

962
00:37:37,421 --> 00:37:38,881
and the members,

963
00:37:39,507 --> 00:37:40,508
amicably.

964
00:37:40,591 --> 00:37:42,593
<i>His eyes look so beautiful.</i>

965
00:37:42,677 --> 00:37:45,012
<i>-Seriously.</i>
<i>-As if they were photoshopped.</i>

966
00:37:45,846 --> 00:37:46,764
It's not hard.

967
00:37:46,847 --> 00:37:47,723
TAKING THE LEAD

968
00:37:47,807 --> 00:37:48,933
HE CAN EVEN SPEED UP

969
00:37:49,016 --> 00:37:50,518
Should we run for a bit?

970
00:37:52,645 --> 00:37:53,813
To be honest,

971
00:37:54,397 --> 00:37:56,482
I haven't been out of breath at all today.

972
00:37:56,565 --> 00:37:58,234
HE HAS GREAT STAMINA

973
00:37:58,317 --> 00:38:00,152
There's a place for food waste?

974
00:38:00,236 --> 00:38:02,071
This ridge is longer than others?

975
00:38:02,154 --> 00:38:05,074
Isn't the wind speed about 3 m/s tomorrow?

976
00:38:05,157 --> 00:38:07,785
If we bring bottled water tomorrow,
won't it freeze?

977
00:38:07,868 --> 00:38:09,078
What do we do on the last day?

978
00:38:09,161 --> 00:38:10,538
So what's the mission?

979
00:38:10,621 --> 00:38:12,248
What happens if we fail?

980
00:38:13,040 --> 00:38:14,208
But…

981
00:38:14,292 --> 00:38:16,335
The Minister of Foreign Affairs keeps…

982
00:38:16,419 --> 00:38:18,879
ASKING THE STAFF COUNTLESS QUESTIONS

983
00:38:18,963 --> 00:38:21,340
UNTIL HE'S OUT OF BREATH

984
00:38:21,424 --> 00:38:23,801
Since when did your eyes look so defiant?

985
00:38:23,884 --> 00:38:26,262
HIS TRUE COLORS
BEHIND THE GOOD-NATURED FACE

986
00:38:26,345 --> 00:38:27,179
Wrong!

987
00:38:27,263 --> 00:38:28,389
Hey, you…

988
00:38:28,472 --> 00:38:30,474
-No.
-You… What's wrong with you?

989
00:38:30,558 --> 00:38:31,517
-Now…
-They're there.

990
00:38:31,600 --> 00:38:32,435
THE YOUNGER MEMBER

991
00:38:32,518 --> 00:38:34,270
What are you talking about?

992
00:38:34,353 --> 00:38:36,230
AND OLDER MEMBERS ARE NO EXCEPTION

993
00:38:36,314 --> 00:38:37,189
What is it?

994
00:38:38,024 --> 00:38:38,941
GLARING

995
00:38:40,026 --> 00:38:42,236
Chae-min's eyes looked so scary just now.

996
00:38:44,488 --> 00:38:46,490
THE TYRANNICAL MINISTER OF FOREIGN AFFAIRS

997
00:38:46,574 --> 00:38:47,575
He's a tyrant.

998
00:38:47,658 --> 00:38:51,579
FULL OF LAUGHTER WHEN THEY ARE NOT HIKING

999
00:38:51,662 --> 00:38:55,333
HERE COMES A STRANGE HIKING CLUB

1000
00:38:55,416 --> 00:38:57,251
"Let's go!" Like this?

1001
00:38:57,918 --> 00:39:00,046
-One, two, three.
-Let's go!

1002
00:39:00,129 --> 00:39:01,922
THE FUTURE OF INVOLUNTARY BEGINNER HIKERS

1003
00:39:05,384 --> 00:39:07,011
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

1004
00:39:07,094 --> 00:39:08,804
JANGGUNBONG

1005
00:39:08,888 --> 00:39:12,183
YEONGCHUKSAN

1006
00:39:12,266 --> 00:39:14,101
Try your best to look close.

1007
00:39:15,728 --> 00:39:16,979
Okay, let's go.

1008
00:39:17,063 --> 00:39:19,815
We can't see Baengnokdam from here.
You don't want to see it?

1009
00:39:19,899 --> 00:39:22,151
THEY ONLY THINK ABOUT GOING DOWN

1010
00:39:22,234 --> 00:39:24,028
-Let's go.
-Let's go!

1011
00:39:24,111 --> 00:39:25,780
THEY'RE HAPPY IF THEY DON'T HIKE

1012
00:39:25,863 --> 00:39:27,114
Why does one go hiking?

1013
00:39:28,074 --> 00:39:29,408
I still don't know.

1014
00:39:29,492 --> 00:39:31,744
WILL THEY BE ABLE TO FIND
THE PURPOSE OF HIKING?

1015
00:39:31,827 --> 00:39:34,246
HIKING IN SEORAKSAN

1016
00:39:35,039 --> 00:39:37,750
BURAMSAN MOUNTAIN, SEOUL

1017
00:39:38,334 --> 00:39:41,003
SOMEONE HAS ARRIVED AT BURAMSAN

1018
00:39:42,755 --> 00:39:43,672
Hello.

1019
00:39:43,756 --> 00:39:46,675
CHAE-MIN CAME TO TRAIN VOLUNTARILY
AS THE INSTRUCTOR ADVISED

1020
00:39:47,385 --> 00:39:48,552
FULL HIKING GEAR

1021
00:39:48,636 --> 00:39:50,054
-It looks good.
-It does?

1022
00:39:50,137 --> 00:39:51,722
-I have a question.
-Okay.

1023
00:39:51,806 --> 00:39:53,641
Should I use the sticks from the start?

1024
00:39:53,724 --> 00:39:55,267
I think you should, as practice.

1025
00:39:55,351 --> 00:39:56,519
Okay, I got it.

1026
00:39:56,602 --> 00:39:59,730
Keep it short when going up,
make it long when coming down.

1027
00:39:59,814 --> 00:40:01,023
-Right.
-You did your homework.

1028
00:40:01,107 --> 00:40:03,526
THE MODEL STUDENT WHO CAME FULLY PREPARED

1029
00:40:03,609 --> 00:40:05,736
Rest step?
There's something like that too.

1030
00:40:06,987 --> 00:40:09,698
I watched some videos
on YouTube yesterday.

1031
00:40:10,616 --> 00:40:12,785
TRAINING IN BURAMSAN BEGINS

1032
00:40:13,994 --> 00:40:17,039
It's been so long
since I last went hiking.

1033
00:40:18,124 --> 00:40:21,419
The mountain we'll be hiking
is about 1,700 m.

1034
00:40:21,502 --> 00:40:22,670
SEORAKSAN ELEVATION: 1,708 M

1035
00:40:22,753 --> 00:40:24,755
It's about five times
as long as today's course.

1036
00:40:24,839 --> 00:40:25,756
PREPPING FOR SEORAKSAN

1037
00:40:26,549 --> 00:40:28,509
I won't have to
work out my legs for a while.

1038
00:40:29,260 --> 00:40:30,428
Hiking will do.

1039
00:40:32,471 --> 00:40:35,266
Your strides are so long, Chae-min.

1040
00:40:37,059 --> 00:40:38,269
STRIDES OF A 190-CM MAN

1041
00:40:38,352 --> 00:40:39,937
So you're so fast.

1042
00:40:41,105 --> 00:40:42,898
FROM WOODEN STEPS

1043
00:40:42,982 --> 00:40:46,318
TO STONE-RIDDLED PATHS, HE HAS NO PROBLEM

1044
00:40:47,319 --> 00:40:50,364
INSTRUCTOR'S ADVICE 1
THE LAYERING SYSTEM

1045
00:40:53,075 --> 00:40:58,664
INSTRUCTOR'S ADVICE 2
DRINKING WATER OFTEN

1046
00:41:01,167 --> 00:41:04,128
INSTRUCTOR'S ADVICE 3
EATING SNACKS TO YOUR LIKING

1047
00:41:04,211 --> 00:41:06,589
The candy tastes sweeter today.

1048
00:41:06,672 --> 00:41:11,135
CLIMBING STEEP SLOPES AS HE STUDIED

1049
00:41:11,218 --> 00:41:12,428
Wow, it's steep.

1050
00:41:13,179 --> 00:41:14,763
This is the steepest part.

1051
00:41:14,847 --> 00:41:20,436
THE LAST HURDLE TO REACH THE TOP

1052
00:41:21,437 --> 00:41:24,815
LOOKING HANDSOME EVEN WITH THE SLOPE

1053
00:41:27,651 --> 00:41:29,653
-Is this the top?
-It is.

1054
00:41:29,737 --> 00:41:31,447
-How many minutes?
-Fifty-five minutes.

1055
00:41:31,530 --> 00:41:33,949
Less than an hour?
Didn't you say it'd take two hours?

1056
00:41:34,033 --> 00:41:36,952
LEE CHAE-MIN'S TRAINING IN BURAMSAN
COMPLETED

1057
00:41:39,079 --> 00:41:41,040
ACHASAN, SEOUL

1058
00:41:41,540 --> 00:41:43,292
Are the trails similar in Seoraksan?

1059
00:41:43,375 --> 00:41:45,503
In the beginning, for about an hour.

1060
00:41:45,586 --> 00:41:48,172
What about after that?
Will I have to find out there?

1061
00:41:48,255 --> 00:41:50,466
At some point, you'll be on all fours.

1062
00:41:50,549 --> 00:41:51,509
Like this.

1063
00:41:52,968 --> 00:41:54,386
FIRST, PRACTICE WALKING ON TWO LEGS

1064
00:41:54,470 --> 00:41:55,763
Slowly. At your own pace.

1065
00:41:56,805 --> 00:42:00,184
LONG STRIDES

1066
00:42:00,267 --> 00:42:02,061
STAFF

1067
00:42:02,144 --> 00:42:05,648
UNEXPECTED
HE'S GOING AHEAD OF THE STAFF

1068
00:42:07,650 --> 00:42:10,611
TWO STEPS AT A TIME

1069
00:42:10,694 --> 00:42:12,071
Why do my hips hurt?

1070
00:42:14,156 --> 00:42:17,201
It proves my poor stamina.

1071
00:42:19,370 --> 00:42:21,080
You've only walked for five minutes.

1072
00:42:22,540 --> 00:42:24,333
Gosh, I get the feeling.

1073
00:42:26,460 --> 00:42:28,754
IT'S NOT EVEN EASY TO WALK ON TWO LEGS

1074
00:42:30,506 --> 00:42:32,591
You have long strides since you're tall.

1075
00:42:32,675 --> 00:42:34,385
HE WALKS FAST, BUT HE'S ALREADY TIRED

1076
00:42:35,177 --> 00:42:37,638
SITS DOWN EVERY CHANCE HE GETS

1077
00:42:38,389 --> 00:42:40,766
STILL, HE KEEPS ON WALKING

1078
00:42:41,475 --> 00:42:43,727
UNBELIEVABLE…

1079
00:42:44,728 --> 00:42:46,564
NOTICEABLY SLOWER ON STEPS

1080
00:42:47,565 --> 00:42:49,149
You can see downtown a bit.

1081
00:42:51,527 --> 00:42:52,736
But you know what?

1082
00:42:53,696 --> 00:42:55,781
I'm not interested in natural scenery.

1083
00:42:58,826 --> 00:43:00,369
When we hike Seoraksan,

1084
00:43:00,995 --> 00:43:02,413
watch my face closely.

1085
00:43:03,247 --> 00:43:04,498
HE KEEPS HIS WORD

1086
00:43:05,708 --> 00:43:07,293
TRUDGING

1087
00:43:07,918 --> 00:43:11,255
HE DOESN'T CARE ABOUT THE SCENERY
AND WON'T TURN AROUND

1088
00:43:15,217 --> 00:43:16,135
It's so tough.

1089
00:43:20,764 --> 00:43:22,683
-Five kilometers from now on.
-Okay.

1090
00:43:23,183 --> 00:43:25,352
DOWOON RUNNING, TARZZAN WORKING OUT

1091
00:43:27,146 --> 00:43:32,443
WITH THE WORLD TOUR AROUND THE CORNER,
HE'S RUNNING AT HANGANG RIVER

1092
00:43:34,778 --> 00:43:39,617
WORKING ABROAD,
TARZZAN IS EXERCISING AT THE GYM

1093
00:43:43,287 --> 00:43:45,247
Why do we go hiking?

1094
00:43:46,874 --> 00:43:49,293
EVERYONE HAS COMPLETED THEIR TRAINING

1095
00:43:51,378 --> 00:43:53,922
SAN 27, SEORAK-DONG,
SOKCHO CITY, GANGWON-DO

1096
00:43:54,006 --> 00:43:56,300
SEORAKSAN SOGONGWON PARK

1097
00:44:01,263 --> 00:44:02,806
SEORAK REST AREA

1098
00:44:02,890 --> 00:44:05,559
CURRENT TEMPERATURE

1099
00:44:09,438 --> 00:44:10,814
Hello.

1100
00:44:10,898 --> 00:44:12,524
TARZZAN ARRIVES

1101
00:44:12,608 --> 00:44:15,319
-He's sagging his pants.
-His pants.

1102
00:44:16,612 --> 00:44:18,906
My butt's going to freeze.

1103
00:44:19,573 --> 00:44:21,116
What's under your nose?

1104
00:44:21,200 --> 00:44:22,618
This?

1105
00:44:22,701 --> 00:44:24,328
It's an acne patch.

1106
00:44:26,497 --> 00:44:30,084
THE PRESIDENT SPRUCED HIMSELF UP

1107
00:44:31,085 --> 00:44:34,254
TILTED

1108
00:44:34,338 --> 00:44:36,298
I can't give up my style.

1109
00:44:36,840 --> 00:44:38,884
THE HIKING BAG HE'S PACKED
FOR THE FIRST TIME

1110
00:44:38,967 --> 00:44:40,010
The essentials.

1111
00:44:42,721 --> 00:44:44,139
Good morning.

1112
00:44:45,808 --> 00:44:47,267
THEY'LL WAIT HERE UNTIL THEY DEPART

1113
00:44:47,351 --> 00:44:48,560
Hello.

1114
00:44:49,645 --> 00:44:51,313
-They'll be here soon.
-Yes.

1115
00:44:55,609 --> 00:45:00,072
FREEZING WEATHER

1116
00:45:00,155 --> 00:45:01,990
Seriously, it's so cold.

1117
00:45:02,991 --> 00:45:04,827
-Hello.
-Hello.

1118
00:45:04,910 --> 00:45:06,286
CHAE-MIN ARRIVES

1119
00:45:06,370 --> 00:45:08,038
-Hello.
-Let's mic up first.

1120
00:45:09,540 --> 00:45:10,874
How are you feeling?

1121
00:45:10,958 --> 00:45:13,001
GRINNING

1122
00:45:13,085 --> 00:45:16,505
It's been so long since I went to bed
early. I couldn't sleep.

1123
00:45:18,882 --> 00:45:21,343
-Maybe I was nervous, or excited.
-Really?

1124
00:45:21,427 --> 00:45:22,761
That's not good.

1125
00:45:23,971 --> 00:45:25,556
Hello.

1126
00:45:26,181 --> 00:45:27,307
Hello.

1127
00:45:27,391 --> 00:45:29,351
-Hello.
-Hello.

1128
00:45:29,435 --> 00:45:31,270
LOOKING UP THE WEATHER FORECAST

1129
00:45:31,353 --> 00:45:32,396
What is it?

1130
00:45:33,647 --> 00:45:34,565
DOWOON ARRIVES

1131
00:45:34,648 --> 00:45:37,025
Is it the sound of the wind? Geez.

1132
00:45:37,734 --> 00:45:38,902
It's insane.

1133
00:45:38,986 --> 00:45:40,696
It feels a lot colder today.

1134
00:45:40,779 --> 00:45:43,240
Right. Why did you pick such a bad day?

1135
00:45:45,117 --> 00:45:47,744
HE'S NOT ON HIS WAY TO AN INTERNET CAFE

1136
00:45:47,828 --> 00:45:49,496
Geez.

1137
00:45:52,458 --> 00:45:57,296
PADDED HAT, PADDED JACKET, PADDED MUFFLER

1138
00:45:58,005 --> 00:46:00,382
THEY'RE STILL LOOKING UP THE FORECAST

1139
00:46:01,133 --> 00:46:03,343
INTERNET CAFE FASHION

1140
00:46:04,761 --> 00:46:05,929
Hello.

1141
00:46:06,013 --> 00:46:07,181
Hey.

1142
00:46:11,894 --> 00:46:13,854
SYMPATHIZING

1143
00:46:13,937 --> 00:46:15,105
Are you all right?

1144
00:46:15,689 --> 00:46:16,690
Are you all right?

1145
00:46:16,773 --> 00:46:18,525
Me? I'm good.

1146
00:46:21,528 --> 00:46:25,657
It's -13.8°C, but it feels like -27.5°C.

1147
00:46:25,741 --> 00:46:27,784
Minus 27.5°C? That's insane.

1148
00:46:27,868 --> 00:46:29,328
Today?

1149
00:46:29,411 --> 00:46:30,746
So why did you pick today?

1150
00:46:30,829 --> 00:46:32,748
Whose idea was this?

1151
00:46:34,541 --> 00:46:37,002
I've never seen -27.5°C before in my life.

1152
00:46:37,085 --> 00:46:37,961
It's -27.5°C?

1153
00:46:38,045 --> 00:46:40,047
-Yes, -27.5°C.
-Right now?

1154
00:46:40,130 --> 00:46:42,090
No one would even go fishing today.

1155
00:46:44,092 --> 00:46:45,093
"Feels like"?

1156
00:46:45,969 --> 00:46:48,138
But -13.8°C is…

1157
00:46:49,973 --> 00:46:51,975
Jung-won isn't here yet?

1158
00:46:53,393 --> 00:46:57,773
CHA JUNG-WON, AKA CAR, THE GARDEN, ARRIVES

1159
00:46:59,024 --> 00:47:02,069
HE LOOKS JUST LIKE A MOUNTAINEER

1160
00:47:07,115 --> 00:47:11,620
HURRYING AS IF BEING CHASED

1161
00:47:11,703 --> 00:47:13,372
Hold on. What about meat?

1162
00:47:13,455 --> 00:47:14,623
We picked up meat.

1163
00:47:15,207 --> 00:47:16,458
Hello.

1164
00:47:16,542 --> 00:47:17,543
Hey.

1165
00:47:17,626 --> 00:47:19,545
You look like a natural mountaineer.

1166
00:47:20,837 --> 00:47:22,089
Gosh, I hate this.

1167
00:47:22,172 --> 00:47:23,423
BEING TEASED RIGHT AWAY

1168
00:47:23,507 --> 00:47:24,841
God, it's so cold.

1169
00:47:25,676 --> 00:47:28,971
Hey, how was it? I heard you went hiking.

1170
00:47:29,054 --> 00:47:30,889
-Achasan was not bad.
-Okay.

1171
00:47:30,973 --> 00:47:34,101
But they say it's nothing
compared to here.

1172
00:47:34,184 --> 00:47:35,018
Really?

1173
00:47:39,940 --> 00:47:41,900
Hey, your eyes look so…

1174
00:47:41,984 --> 00:47:43,277
unenthusiastic.

1175
00:47:44,194 --> 00:47:47,030
What? Don't you remember
what you texted me last night?

1176
00:47:47,114 --> 00:47:48,156
"I'm so worried."

1177
00:47:48,240 --> 00:47:49,950
COWARD

1178
00:47:50,033 --> 00:47:51,868
And you, you went to church yesterday.

1179
00:47:51,952 --> 00:47:54,746
Yes, I prayed
that I would come back down safely.

1180
00:47:56,748 --> 00:47:59,501
We looked up
today's weather forecast earlier.

1181
00:47:59,585 --> 00:48:03,088
The wind chill is about -27°C.

1182
00:48:03,171 --> 00:48:04,840
-I've never heard it before.
-Right.

1183
00:48:04,923 --> 00:48:09,970
And the real temperature outside is -13°C.

1184
00:48:11,555 --> 00:48:13,015
This is so frustrating.

1185
00:48:14,349 --> 00:48:16,643
I talked to ChatGPT yesterday.

1186
00:48:16,727 --> 00:48:19,313
And it knows I'm Car, the garden.

1187
00:48:20,147 --> 00:48:21,523
And I…

1188
00:48:21,607 --> 00:48:25,027
It's Huiungak Shelter that's here, right?

1189
00:48:25,110 --> 00:48:28,655
I asked if I'd be okay going there,
saying it was my first time.

1190
00:48:29,948 --> 00:48:33,243
It said, "No matter
how hot Producer Nah is

1191
00:48:33,327 --> 00:48:37,122
and how helpful you think it'll be,
I think you should cancel it."

1192
00:48:37,205 --> 00:48:38,790
-Come on.
-I said, "Really?"

1193
00:48:38,874 --> 00:48:41,418
"Will I have to pay a penalty fee?"

1194
00:48:41,501 --> 00:48:43,378
It said, "Should I look it up for you?"

1195
00:48:44,171 --> 00:48:46,465
ChatGPT tried to dissuade me twice.

1196
00:48:46,548 --> 00:48:47,841
-Really?
-Yes.

1197
00:48:48,467 --> 00:48:50,260
TODAY'S TRAIL

1198
00:48:50,344 --> 00:48:52,220
The trail we'll take is

1199
00:48:52,304 --> 00:48:54,848
Cheonbuldonggyegok Valley Trail

1200
00:48:54,931 --> 00:48:57,017
that ends at Huiungak Shelter.

1201
00:48:57,100 --> 00:48:59,603
CHEONBULDONGGYEGOK VALLEY TRAIL

1202
00:48:59,686 --> 00:49:03,357
SEORAKSAN'S VALLEYS AND RUGGED PRECIPICE
MAKE BEAUTIFUL SCENERY

1203
00:49:03,440 --> 00:49:07,069
IT'S ONE OF THE MAIN TRAILS
KNOWN FOR BEAUTIFUL AUTUMN FOLIAGE

1204
00:49:10,739 --> 00:49:14,534
FINAL DESTINATION: HUIUNGAK SHELTER

1205
00:49:15,243 --> 00:49:19,039
It is going to take
a little less than five hours going up.

1206
00:49:19,873 --> 00:49:21,958
And about ten hours round-trip.

1207
00:49:22,042 --> 00:49:25,128
And it's about 17 km.

1208
00:49:25,796 --> 00:49:27,297
SEORAKSAN SOGONGWON FRONT GATE

1209
00:49:27,381 --> 00:49:29,174
GWIMYEONAM ROCK

1210
00:49:29,257 --> 00:49:32,719
HUIUNGAK SHELTER

1211
00:49:32,803 --> 00:49:37,057
<i>For the first hour, the walk will be easy.</i>

1212
00:49:37,140 --> 00:49:39,726
<i>In the middle, it'll get a bit tougher.</i>

1213
00:49:39,810 --> 00:49:41,895
<i>And for the last two hours,</i>

1214
00:49:41,978 --> 00:49:45,190
<i>a very challenging trail awaits you.</i>

1215
00:49:45,273 --> 00:49:49,361
IT'LL BE A HARD JOURNEY
FOR THE BEGINNER HIKERS

1216
00:49:49,444 --> 00:49:51,405
So that's our plan.

1217
00:49:51,488 --> 00:49:53,782
And since today's our first filming,

1218
00:49:53,865 --> 00:49:56,576
let me briefly explain

1219
00:49:56,660 --> 00:49:59,413
the system of our show, <i>Take a Hike!</i>

1220
00:49:59,496 --> 00:50:04,084
We're going to conquer the most symbolic

1221
00:50:04,167 --> 00:50:07,587
and beautiful mountains in Korea

1222
00:50:07,671 --> 00:50:09,089
one by one.

1223
00:50:39,369 --> 00:50:43,290
We wanted to test you
to see if you're ready for the quest.

1224
00:50:43,373 --> 00:50:46,543
So we picked this mountain
that's not included in the quest.

1225
00:50:46,626 --> 00:50:48,253
-What?
-What?

1226
00:50:48,837 --> 00:50:49,838
Today,

1227
00:50:50,964 --> 00:50:52,799
just consider it

1228
00:50:52,883 --> 00:50:55,886
as pre-season training.

1229
00:50:55,969 --> 00:50:58,221
I mean, we're not even going
for the summit.

1230
00:50:58,305 --> 00:50:59,389
Just the shelter.

1231
00:50:59,473 --> 00:51:01,349
We'll just touch the shelter
and come down.

1232
00:51:01,433 --> 00:51:04,978
So after seeing how well you hike today,

1233
00:51:05,061 --> 00:51:08,774
we'll decide
how we'll give you the next one and when.

1234
00:51:08,857 --> 00:51:10,650
We can't let just anyone do it.

1235
00:51:10,734 --> 00:51:12,986
They might get hurt
or get into an accident.

1236
00:51:13,695 --> 00:51:15,071
I'm that "just anyone."

1237
00:51:16,448 --> 00:51:18,825
I'm no one special. I'm nothing.

1238
00:51:20,368 --> 00:51:21,536
Seriously, I…

1239
00:51:21,620 --> 00:51:23,705
JUST ANYONE

1240
00:51:25,165 --> 00:51:27,667
What's important is
that we shouldn't do too well today.

1241
00:51:28,585 --> 00:51:29,586
"Shouldn't"?

1242
00:51:29,669 --> 00:51:31,171
Let's collapse halfway.

1243
00:51:32,964 --> 00:51:35,258
Then some of us
might get eliminated today?

1244
00:51:35,926 --> 00:51:37,469
If you do badly.

1245
00:51:37,552 --> 00:51:38,970
Is it a survival show?

1246
00:51:39,054 --> 00:51:41,807
This, plus survival? That's absurd.

1247
00:51:41,890 --> 00:51:43,934
You might be able to drop out.

1248
00:51:44,017 --> 00:51:45,018
INTRIGUED

1249
00:51:45,101 --> 00:51:46,311
That's what you want.

1250
00:51:47,062 --> 00:51:49,356
HIS WISH: DROPPING OUT

1251
00:51:49,439 --> 00:51:51,358
5 MINUTES BEFORE DEPARTURE

1252
00:51:52,359 --> 00:51:54,986
I never thought
I'd do a show about hiking.

1253
00:51:57,864 --> 00:52:00,325
And why did it have to be with us?

1254
00:52:02,536 --> 00:52:03,995
You thought the same, right?

1255
00:52:04,079 --> 00:52:05,497
Be honest.

1256
00:52:05,580 --> 00:52:07,457
I almost said it out loud but held it.

1257
00:52:07,541 --> 00:52:08,917
Because it's pointless now.

1258
00:52:09,000 --> 00:52:10,043
It's too late?

1259
00:52:10,126 --> 00:52:12,295
NO BACKSIES

1260
00:52:12,379 --> 00:52:17,133
HIKING BEGINS

1261
00:52:17,217 --> 00:52:18,718
Look, the sun's rising.

1262
00:52:18,802 --> 00:52:20,303
It feels nice.

1263
00:52:20,387 --> 00:52:21,972
I suddenly feel so good.

1264
00:52:23,682 --> 00:52:26,017
It's been a while
since I was awake at this hour.

1265
00:52:27,269 --> 00:52:29,229
I'll take a photo now. I'll be quick.

1266
00:52:29,312 --> 00:52:31,022
You can look here.

1267
00:52:31,106 --> 00:52:32,899
TAKING PICTURES IS A MUST WHEN HIKING

1268
00:52:32,983 --> 00:52:34,359
Look at the camera.

1269
00:52:34,442 --> 00:52:36,695
THEY DON'T WANT TO DO IT

1270
00:52:36,778 --> 00:52:38,029
One more time.

1271
00:52:39,155 --> 00:52:40,448
Say "let's go!"

1272
00:52:40,532 --> 00:52:41,867
"Let's go!" Like this.

1273
00:52:42,576 --> 00:52:44,244
Now, one, two, three.

1274
00:52:44,327 --> 00:52:45,495
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

1275
00:52:46,121 --> 00:52:48,039
-One, two, three.
-Let's go!

1276
00:52:51,251 --> 00:52:54,754
AT SEORAKSAN SOGONGWON PARK
ON JAN 12, 2026

1277
00:52:54,838 --> 00:52:56,172
What is this?

1278
00:52:56,256 --> 00:52:58,550
THEY FIND IT RIDICULOUS

1279
00:53:00,051 --> 00:53:01,636
It's not as cold as I expected.

1280
00:53:01,720 --> 00:53:03,763
CONDUCTED UNDER THE SUPERVISION
OF PROFESSIONALS

1281
00:53:03,847 --> 00:53:05,473
-Compared to before…
-Is it better?

1282
00:53:06,766 --> 00:53:10,020
SEORAKSAN SOGONGWON FRONT GATE

1283
00:53:14,107 --> 00:53:16,651
I didn't know
the sticks would feel so awkward.

1284
00:53:17,235 --> 00:53:19,154
You must think they're your own legs.

1285
00:53:21,573 --> 00:53:23,325
Hey, the screen's not even on yet.

1286
00:53:23,408 --> 00:53:25,660
Exactly. My goodness.

1287
00:53:26,953 --> 00:53:29,414
Then maybe we're the first hikers today.

1288
00:53:30,206 --> 00:53:32,083
The paths will be like this until the end?

1289
00:53:32,167 --> 00:53:33,543
No. Never.

1290
00:53:34,336 --> 00:53:36,087
-"Never."
-I've only been to Namsan.

1291
00:53:36,171 --> 00:53:37,631
That'd be so nice.

1292
00:53:37,714 --> 00:53:38,840
THE INEXPERIENCED PRESIDENT

1293
00:53:38,924 --> 00:53:40,634
Wow, that must be it.

1294
00:53:41,551 --> 00:53:42,719
It is beautiful.

1295
00:53:45,138 --> 00:53:46,556
It's still snowy.

1296
00:53:46,640 --> 00:53:48,183
It's so beautiful.

1297
00:53:49,476 --> 00:53:50,769
I really enjoyed it.

1298
00:53:51,645 --> 00:53:52,896
Ending now would be perfect.

1299
00:53:52,979 --> 00:53:55,982
You know, if you grill meat here,
it tastes even better.

1300
00:53:56,066 --> 00:53:58,109
LUNCH: PORK BELLY

1301
00:53:58,193 --> 00:53:59,319
Seriously.

1302
00:53:59,402 --> 00:54:01,571
Wow, it's so pretty over there.

1303
00:54:01,655 --> 00:54:03,782
I think the cable cars
must be around here.

1304
00:54:03,865 --> 00:54:06,660
Yes, Kwon Geumseong on your left

1305
00:54:06,743 --> 00:54:08,495
is where the cable car goes up.

1306
00:54:08,578 --> 00:54:09,829
HERE

1307
00:54:09,913 --> 00:54:11,373
SEORAKSAN CABLE CAR

1308
00:54:11,456 --> 00:54:14,542
YOU CAN GO UP
TO KWON GEUMSEONG COMFORTABLY

1309
00:54:14,626 --> 00:54:17,128
AND ENJOY THE MAGNIFICENT SCENERY

1310
00:54:18,463 --> 00:54:20,674
KWON GEUMSEONG FORTRESS

1311
00:54:21,424 --> 00:54:24,260
NOJEOKBONG PEAK & TOWANGSEONGPOKPO FALLS

1312
00:54:24,886 --> 00:54:27,681
STRONG WIND

1313
00:54:28,390 --> 00:54:29,391
It's so cold.

1314
00:54:29,474 --> 00:54:31,101
-So cold.
-So cold.

1315
00:54:31,851 --> 00:54:33,269
Wow, my face feels so cold.

1316
00:54:33,353 --> 00:54:34,980
-Me too.
-I should cover it.

1317
00:54:36,147 --> 00:54:38,024
PUTTING ON THE BALACLAVA

1318
00:54:38,108 --> 00:54:39,818
Maybe I should've brought that too.

1319
00:54:40,986 --> 00:54:42,862
Now that I've covered my face,

1320
00:54:43,989 --> 00:54:44,906
it's much better.

1321
00:54:45,782 --> 00:54:47,534
THE TWO WHO BROUGHT BALACLAVAS

1322
00:54:47,617 --> 00:54:49,327
I should've brought one.

1323
00:54:49,411 --> 00:54:50,912
THE TWO WHO DIDN'T

1324
00:54:52,789 --> 00:54:54,165
It's definitely better.

1325
00:54:55,000 --> 00:54:56,584
-Definitely better.
-Definitely.

1326
00:54:56,668 --> 00:54:59,671
You're still not true celebs.
You shouldn't cover your faces.

1327
00:55:00,588 --> 00:55:01,756
Cameras are rolling.

1328
00:55:01,840 --> 00:55:02,799
Thank you!

1329
00:55:02,882 --> 00:55:05,635
6TH YEAR, 2ND YEAR, 12TH YEAR, 14TH YEAR

1330
00:55:05,719 --> 00:55:07,846
But I think it's okay
for me to cover mine.

1331
00:55:08,972 --> 00:55:11,933
This is Sinheungsa Temple.
You're going through Sinheungsa.

1332
00:55:12,559 --> 00:55:15,020
There's a big statue
of the Buddha on your right.

1333
00:55:15,645 --> 00:55:16,771
Wow, it's huge.

1334
00:55:21,609 --> 00:55:24,195
SINHEUNGSA TEMPLE

1335
00:55:24,779 --> 00:55:27,449
A HISTORIC TEMPLE SITUATED
ON THE SLOPES OF SEORAKSAN

1336
00:55:27,532 --> 00:55:30,952
KNOWN FOR ITS PEACEFUL AMBIENCE
AND BIG BRONZE STATUE OF THE BUDDHA

1337
00:55:31,661 --> 00:55:33,038
Well, I'm a Christian.

1338
00:55:34,706 --> 00:55:36,833
But I'm sure they're close.

1339
00:55:36,916 --> 00:55:38,626
God and the Buddha? Of course.

1340
00:55:39,753 --> 00:55:41,212
We'll be back safely.

1341
00:55:42,380 --> 00:55:44,215
Please wish us luck.

1342
00:55:44,299 --> 00:55:45,175
PRAYING

1343
00:55:45,258 --> 00:55:48,219
What you see on your right
is Ulsanbawi Rock.

1344
00:55:49,262 --> 00:55:50,555
My hometown, Ulsan.

1345
00:55:57,979 --> 00:56:01,816
ULSANBAWI ROCK

1346
00:56:02,942 --> 00:56:06,196
ONE OF THE MOST SYMBOLIC ATTRACTIONS
OF SEORAKSAN

1347
00:56:06,279 --> 00:56:09,741
THE HUGE SAWTOOTH-LIKE ROCKY PEAKS
PRESENT A GRAND SITE

1348
00:56:13,912 --> 00:56:17,624
On your left, a lot of snow has piled up
on the summit.

1349
00:56:18,291 --> 00:56:19,626
Is that Daecheongbong Peak?

1350
00:56:20,710 --> 00:56:21,795
It is.

1351
00:56:21,878 --> 00:56:22,921
-That one?
-Yes.

1352
00:56:23,505 --> 00:56:25,298
-Are we going there?
-No, not there.

1353
00:56:25,381 --> 00:56:27,550
On your left. We're not going there,

1354
00:56:27,634 --> 00:56:29,719
but our destination is on the way there.

1355
00:56:34,808 --> 00:56:38,812
DAECHEONGBONG PEAK

1356
00:56:38,895 --> 00:56:42,774
THE HIGHEST AND MOST SYMBOLIC PEAK
IN SEORAKSAN

1357
00:56:42,857 --> 00:56:46,569
YOU CAN ENJOY THE SCENERY
OF THE MAGNIFICENT TERRAIN

1358
00:56:46,653 --> 00:56:50,365
AND THE VIEW STRETCHING TO THE EAST SEA

1359
00:56:55,120 --> 00:57:00,041
DAECHEONGBONG

1360
00:57:02,085 --> 00:57:03,378
My problem is,

1361
00:57:04,003 --> 00:57:05,588
I'm not interested

1362
00:57:05,672 --> 00:57:07,966
-in natural scenery.
-Seriously?

1363
00:57:08,049 --> 00:57:11,427
So when I went hiking in Seoul,
the staff were like,

1364
00:57:11,511 --> 00:57:13,721
"You can see downtown Seoul from here."

1365
00:57:13,805 --> 00:57:16,641
But I was just not interested at all.

1366
00:57:18,518 --> 00:57:20,520
I just don't care about it.

1367
00:57:20,603 --> 00:57:23,690
I used to fight with my ex-girlfriends
a lot because of it.

1368
00:57:24,774 --> 00:57:27,360
"Then why did we come here?"
"Because you wanted to."

1369
00:57:28,695 --> 00:57:31,281
And the question
I'm least interested in is

1370
00:57:31,364 --> 00:57:32,949
"Do you like mountains or the sea?"

1371
00:57:33,741 --> 00:57:35,618
Only the accommodation matters to me.

1372
00:57:39,831 --> 00:57:41,833
Surely, snowy mountains will be different.

1373
00:57:43,168 --> 00:57:44,586
I bet they are.

1374
00:57:45,670 --> 00:57:48,465
SINHEUNGSA TEMPLE

1375
00:57:48,548 --> 00:57:49,799
DIFFICULTY: EASY

1376
00:57:49,883 --> 00:57:52,385
You'll walk like this
for another 30 minutes.

1377
00:57:54,137 --> 00:57:55,096
The air is so fresh.

1378
00:57:55,722 --> 00:57:56,598
It's nice.

1379
00:57:57,849 --> 00:57:59,893
That's a perfect uphill trail.

1380
00:57:59,976 --> 00:58:00,977
Right.

1381
00:58:01,060 --> 00:58:02,103
Like this,

1382
00:58:02,896 --> 00:58:03,855
I can keep going.

1383
00:58:03,938 --> 00:58:06,065
-Seriously, even for ten hours.
-Yes.

1384
00:58:06,816 --> 00:58:09,611
HOWEVER

1385
00:58:09,694 --> 00:58:12,155
All right, the paved trail ends here.

1386
00:58:12,238 --> 00:58:13,323
-Okay.
-Okay.

1387
00:58:13,406 --> 00:58:15,825
PROPER HIKING TRAILS BEGIN HERE

1388
00:58:16,409 --> 00:58:18,620
STRIDING

1389
00:58:18,703 --> 00:58:20,914
We must be quick walkers indeed.

1390
00:58:22,207 --> 00:58:24,083
Right. You're just
walking normally, right?

1391
00:58:24,167 --> 00:58:25,168
Yes.

1392
00:58:25,251 --> 00:58:27,003
I bet you normally walk faster.

1393
00:58:27,086 --> 00:58:28,922
Yes. I'm trying my best to keep pace.

1394
00:58:29,005 --> 00:58:30,089
Oh, really?

1395
00:58:31,841 --> 00:58:33,760
-Let's keep pace with Tarzzan.
-Okay.

1396
00:58:33,843 --> 00:58:35,428
TARZZAN

1397
00:58:35,512 --> 00:58:37,555
It's just the beginning.

1398
00:58:39,432 --> 00:58:41,392
-You're feeling it, right?
-Yes.

1399
00:58:42,894 --> 00:58:44,604
I feel it right away. So annoying.

1400
00:58:45,939 --> 00:58:48,691
I think it'll be hard to talk later.
It's so cold.

1401
00:58:48,775 --> 00:58:51,319
-My lips already feel stiff.
-Me too.

1402
00:58:52,195 --> 00:58:54,572
My mouth is freezing, and it's exhausting.

1403
00:58:55,198 --> 00:58:57,492
Let's talk a lot when we come down.

1404
00:58:58,117 --> 00:59:01,663
I think we can save chatting
for when we're back down.

1405
00:59:02,497 --> 00:59:03,748
I'll explain it briefly.

1406
00:59:04,332 --> 00:59:06,543
These rocks here.

1407
00:59:06,626 --> 00:59:08,503
They're called "Kissing Rocks."

1408
00:59:08,586 --> 00:59:09,629
Oh, right.

1409
00:59:10,421 --> 00:59:11,965
All right, let's move on.

1410
00:59:13,508 --> 00:59:15,343
Don't make us stop
for something like that.

1411
00:59:17,053 --> 00:59:18,137
"Kissing Rocks"?

1412
00:59:27,313 --> 00:59:29,107
I mean, don't we

1413
00:59:29,899 --> 00:59:31,442
look like trainees in boot camp?

1414
00:59:32,193 --> 00:59:33,027
Right.

1415
00:59:33,611 --> 00:59:34,487
WEEK 4 TRAINING MARCH

1416
00:59:34,571 --> 00:59:36,823
-They're different ages, right?
-Exactly.

1417
00:59:38,324 --> 00:59:40,326
This is called "Waseondae."

1418
00:59:41,244 --> 00:59:42,161
"Waseondae"?

1419
00:59:43,788 --> 00:59:45,123
Yes, Waseondae,

1420
00:59:45,206 --> 00:59:49,794
because it's said that a hermit
once lay here admiring the scenery.

1421
00:59:49,877 --> 00:59:52,297
So where did the hermit lie?

1422
00:59:53,172 --> 00:59:55,216
-Where?
-I think it's the rock over there.

1423
00:59:55,300 --> 00:59:58,720
If we go up further, there's a wide rock.
Just a bit further.

1424
00:59:59,929 --> 01:00:02,181
I think this rock is Waseondae.

1425
01:00:04,434 --> 01:00:06,102
You think, or you're sure?

1426
01:00:06,185 --> 01:00:07,020
I'm sure.

1427
01:00:07,103 --> 01:00:08,021
BAD DOCENT

1428
01:00:08,104 --> 01:00:09,355
They all look the same.

1429
01:00:10,481 --> 01:00:11,816
Very well.

1430
01:00:14,027 --> 01:00:15,820
MEANWHILE

1431
01:00:15,903 --> 01:00:18,698
THE STATUS OF PRESIDENT TAR'S PANTS

1432
01:00:20,283 --> 01:00:24,412
THE WORLD'S FIRST HIKER WITH SAGGING PANTS

1433
01:00:25,663 --> 01:00:27,290
I bet his butt's freezing.

1434
01:00:28,416 --> 01:00:29,459
Right.

1435
01:00:30,043 --> 01:00:31,210
-Tarzzan.
-Yes?

1436
01:00:31,294 --> 01:00:32,545
Your butt's not cold?

1437
01:00:32,629 --> 01:00:36,549
No, the pants inside are warmer.
The ones outside are thin.

1438
01:00:36,633 --> 01:00:37,800
-Is that so?
-Yes.

1439
01:00:39,218 --> 01:00:40,928
The pants are too big for me.

1440
01:00:41,012 --> 01:00:42,013
I see.

1441
01:00:45,767 --> 01:00:47,894
-That's so cute.
-It's very hip hop.

1442
01:00:50,021 --> 01:00:52,899
What you see on your right
is Biseondae Rock. We'll head toward it.

1443
01:00:52,982 --> 01:00:54,192
THE EASY PART IS OVER

1444
01:00:56,069 --> 01:00:57,487
The wind's getting colder.

1445
01:00:58,321 --> 01:01:00,239
Without trees, it's so windy.

1446
01:01:00,740 --> 01:01:02,450
Gosh, my face is freezing.

1447
01:01:04,702 --> 01:01:08,831
CURRENT WIND DIRECTION: WEST
SPEED: 15.9 M/S

1448
01:01:12,669 --> 01:01:15,672
THE VALLEY'S FROZEN DUE TO A COLD WAVE

1449
01:01:16,881 --> 01:01:20,802
WITH WIND GETTING STRONGER

1450
01:01:21,719 --> 01:01:24,806
IT FEELS BLEAK

1451
01:01:24,889 --> 01:01:28,184
When I walked through the valley,

1452
01:01:28,267 --> 01:01:31,396
I felt a bit afraid.

1453
01:01:32,689 --> 01:01:35,608
And I also felt overwhelmed
by Mother Nature.

1454
01:01:37,026 --> 01:01:38,569
Wow, it's frozen hard.

1455
01:01:41,322 --> 01:01:42,615
It's all frozen.

1456
01:01:45,201 --> 01:01:52,166
CONTINUOUS STEPS ALONG THE VALLEY

1457
01:01:54,627 --> 01:01:55,962
Damn steps.

1458
01:01:57,296 --> 01:01:59,340
<i>What did you think of your pace?</i>

1459
01:01:59,424 --> 01:02:02,009
-It was good in the beginning.
-It was?

1460
01:02:02,093 --> 01:02:04,178
-I thought I could get through it.
-However…

1461
01:02:04,262 --> 01:02:05,888
Then it got harder and harder.

1462
01:02:05,972 --> 01:02:06,848
Yes.

1463
01:02:09,642 --> 01:02:11,102
One, two, three.

1464
01:02:11,185 --> 01:02:14,397
THIS IS THE PRELUDE TO GREAT SUFFERING

1465
01:02:14,480 --> 01:02:17,567
1 HOUR INTO HIKING
THEY ARRIVE AT BISEONDAE ROCK

1466
01:02:18,359 --> 01:02:19,736
This is an easy course?

1467
01:02:19,819 --> 01:02:21,946
No, it's moderate.

1468
01:02:22,029 --> 01:02:24,574
DIFFICULTY: MODERATE

1469
01:02:24,657 --> 01:02:27,034
FLAT TRAIL

1470
01:02:28,161 --> 01:02:30,163
METAL STEPS

1471
01:02:31,539 --> 01:02:35,209
ROCKY STEPS

1472
01:02:35,752 --> 01:02:38,713
THE EVER-CHANGING PATH OF A MODERATE TRAIL

1473
01:02:39,881 --> 01:02:42,633
LEAD: CAR, THE GARDEN

1474
01:02:43,301 --> 01:02:45,636
MIDDLE 1: DOWOON

1475
01:02:46,596 --> 01:02:49,098
MIDDLE 2: TARZZAN

1476
01:02:49,932 --> 01:02:52,393
TAIL: CHAE-MIN

1477
01:02:52,977 --> 01:02:55,521
1ST LINEUP OF SEORAKSAN HIKING

1478
01:02:57,148 --> 01:02:58,357
Is the pace good?

1479
01:02:58,900 --> 01:03:00,568
-I can just keep going, right?
-Yes.

1480
01:03:00,651 --> 01:03:01,736
It's good.

1481
01:03:01,819 --> 01:03:02,862
It's not that fast.

1482
01:03:02,945 --> 01:03:04,572
You can go faster if you want.

1483
01:03:05,823 --> 01:03:07,575
Don't worry about us.

1484
01:03:07,658 --> 01:03:08,868
But I'm tired.

1485
01:03:09,994 --> 01:03:11,037
Already.

1486
01:03:12,455 --> 01:03:19,086
LOW STAMINA, FAST WALKER

1487
01:03:21,589 --> 01:03:24,926
BUT HE GOES SLOW ON STEPS

1488
01:03:27,345 --> 01:03:32,475
"A HIGHLY SKILLED MOUNTAINEER
TAKES HIS TIME

1489
01:03:32,558 --> 01:03:39,023
AND ALWAYS CLIMBS AT HIS OWN PACE."
-FRANK SMYTHE

1490
01:03:41,776 --> 01:03:42,819
Damn it.

1491
01:03:44,570 --> 01:03:47,448
STEPS YET AGAIN

1492
01:03:51,410 --> 01:03:57,708
"ALPINISM IS THE ART OF SUFFERING."
-VOYTEK KURTYKA

1493
01:04:02,713 --> 01:04:04,257
"OVER EVERY MOUNTAIN, THERE IS A PATH,

1494
01:04:04,340 --> 01:04:06,968
ALTHOUGH IT MAY NOT BE SEEN
FROM THE VALLEY." -THEODORE ROETHKE

1495
01:04:08,094 --> 01:04:09,303
Watch for snow.

1496
01:04:12,014 --> 01:04:18,604
AN ICY SECTION BEGINS

1497
01:04:18,688 --> 01:04:20,314
Wow, there's snow now.

1498
01:04:33,494 --> 01:04:35,621
SLIPPERY

1499
01:04:38,583 --> 01:04:41,377
SLIP

1500
01:04:41,460 --> 01:04:45,131
We'll put on crampons after this part.
They say it's getting icier.

1501
01:04:52,138 --> 01:04:53,472
Be careful of this rock.

1502
01:04:59,353 --> 01:05:00,771
-Be careful here.
-Okay.

1503
01:05:04,317 --> 01:05:08,529
1 HOUR AND 15 MINUTES INTO HIKING
THEY PUT ON CRAMPONS

1504
01:05:08,613 --> 01:05:10,364
WHAT ARE CRAMPONS?

1505
01:05:14,243 --> 01:05:16,704
TRACTION DEVICES
CONSISTING OF METAL SPIKES

1506
01:05:16,787 --> 01:05:19,498
PUT ON OVER HIKING BOOTS
TO PREVENT SLIPPING

1507
01:05:19,582 --> 01:05:20,583
-Like this?
-Yes.

1508
01:05:20,666 --> 01:05:21,918
-This is correct?
-Yes.

1509
01:05:25,171 --> 01:05:27,381
-Is this right?
-Yes, all the way.

1510
01:05:31,719 --> 01:05:34,305
The grip sure is much better.

1511
01:05:34,388 --> 01:05:36,015
CHAE-MIN PRACTICED IT IN BURAMSAN

1512
01:05:36,974 --> 01:05:39,268
THE PROPER WAY TO PUT ON CRAMPONS

1513
01:05:39,352 --> 01:05:40,478
All done.

1514
01:05:42,104 --> 01:05:44,815
MEANWHILE, IT'S THE FIRST TIME
FOR PRESIDENT TAR

1515
01:05:45,399 --> 01:05:47,109
GIVING IT A TRY WITH PASSION

1516
01:05:53,491 --> 01:05:55,076
It sure feels different.

1517
01:05:56,243 --> 01:05:57,536
You did well.

1518
01:05:57,620 --> 01:05:59,246
Of course. I practiced.

1519
01:05:59,330 --> 01:06:00,539
-You did?
-Yes.

1520
01:06:02,541 --> 01:06:04,126
I can't see my face.

1521
01:06:04,210 --> 01:06:05,795
CHECKING HIS APPEARANCE BRIEFLY

1522
01:06:05,878 --> 01:06:07,046
Does it feel like hiking now?

1523
01:06:07,880 --> 01:06:09,090
Well, it's fun.

1524
01:06:10,591 --> 01:06:12,551
It's tough. It's been a while.

1525
01:06:14,345 --> 01:06:16,764
How are you feeling, guys? Are you okay?

1526
01:06:16,847 --> 01:06:17,765
It's tough.

1527
01:06:20,393 --> 01:06:21,852
Everyone's talking less.

1528
01:06:21,936 --> 01:06:23,104
You look okay. Is it doable?

1529
01:06:23,896 --> 01:06:25,731
It's not bad. Better than I thought.

1530
01:06:26,565 --> 01:06:28,776
THEY SET OUT AGAIN

1531
01:06:28,859 --> 01:06:29,944
-You okay?
-Yes.

1532
01:06:30,027 --> 01:06:30,987
It sure is different.

1533
01:06:31,070 --> 01:06:32,822
It was so slippery earlier.

1534
01:06:32,905 --> 01:06:33,823
Right.

1535
01:06:35,825 --> 01:06:36,951
Wow, it's good.

1536
01:06:38,828 --> 01:06:43,207
A DOWNHILL PART RIGHT AWAY

1537
01:06:43,290 --> 01:06:44,333
It's not slippery now.

1538
01:06:44,417 --> 01:06:46,919
AMAZED

1539
01:06:47,003 --> 01:06:48,254
The grip's insane.

1540
01:06:49,422 --> 01:06:50,715
It feels like I'm wearing

1541
01:06:51,716 --> 01:06:52,800
those spike shoes.

1542
01:06:54,802 --> 01:06:56,387
Doesn't it feel so soft?

1543
01:06:56,470 --> 01:06:58,180
Yes, it feels so nice.

1544
01:06:58,931 --> 01:07:01,183
It feels so soft on the ground.

1545
01:07:03,310 --> 01:07:07,690
I realized that they were essentials
when there was snow.

1546
01:07:08,399 --> 01:07:10,234
Honestly, when I packed my bag,

1547
01:07:10,317 --> 01:07:13,988
I thought, "I'm not climbing
the Himalayas. I wouldn't be using them."

1548
01:07:14,071 --> 01:07:17,199
But wow, they were lifesavers for me.

1549
01:07:18,159 --> 01:07:20,453
-This sure is different.
-It's so good.

1550
01:07:21,370 --> 01:07:23,372
I'm more stable now.

1551
01:07:23,456 --> 01:07:24,498
I feel like

1552
01:07:25,499 --> 01:07:27,543
my stamina's being recharged.

1553
01:07:29,003 --> 01:07:30,421
New items acquired.

1554
01:07:31,714 --> 01:07:33,466
<i>I realized they were a must.</i>

1555
01:07:34,216 --> 01:07:36,719
They say the right equipment
can be very helpful.

1556
01:07:36,802 --> 01:07:38,971
That's especially true in snowy mountains.

1557
01:07:41,098 --> 01:07:42,391
I'm getting hungry.

1558
01:07:43,100 --> 01:07:44,518
-Right?
-I'm feeling hungry.

1559
01:07:44,602 --> 01:07:45,603
I'm hungry.

1560
01:07:47,188 --> 01:07:49,523
-Are we halfway there now?
-Halfway?

1561
01:07:50,441 --> 01:07:51,609
Not halfway yet.

1562
01:07:52,151 --> 01:07:53,944
SIGHS

1563
01:07:58,908 --> 01:08:01,911
MEANWHILE, CHAE-MIN'S POINT OF VIEW

1564
01:08:03,662 --> 01:08:08,709
SAGGING

1565
01:08:11,003 --> 01:08:13,839
I watched his butt
the whole time I was climbing.

1566
01:08:15,841 --> 01:08:17,134
And he didn't give it up.

1567
01:08:17,760 --> 01:08:19,512
But that's commendable.

1568
01:08:19,595 --> 01:08:23,224
I wanted to look better and cooler too,

1569
01:08:24,350 --> 01:08:26,268
but I didn't have the energy.

1570
01:08:26,352 --> 01:08:28,646
It was just so tough as it was.

1571
01:08:28,729 --> 01:08:30,064
But he…

1572
01:08:31,607 --> 01:08:33,526
He still had the energy to pull it up.

1573
01:08:35,486 --> 01:08:38,656
ONCE

1574
01:08:38,739 --> 01:08:41,784
TWICE

1575
01:08:41,867 --> 01:08:45,329
927TH TIME

1576
01:08:45,412 --> 01:08:50,126
20,020,927TH TIME

1577
01:08:50,209 --> 01:08:52,086
<i>The pants…</i>

1578
01:08:52,169 --> 01:08:55,047
I didn't mean to sag them.

1579
01:08:55,131 --> 01:08:57,967
I was going to wear
just one layer of pants,

1580
01:08:58,759 --> 01:09:00,302
but it felt so cold.

1581
01:09:00,386 --> 01:09:02,930
So I wore another pair of sweatpants
and then the pants.

1582
01:09:03,597 --> 01:09:04,682
But the problem was,

1583
01:09:04,765 --> 01:09:07,810
it was hard to know
the pants were slipping down,

1584
01:09:07,893 --> 01:09:10,521
and Chae-min kept telling me
they were slipping down,

1585
01:09:10,604 --> 01:09:11,689
so I kept pulling them up.

1586
01:09:11,772 --> 01:09:15,734
I was never doing it intentionally
to try to look cool.

1587
01:09:15,818 --> 01:09:18,070
Never. Please don't misunderstand.

1588
01:09:22,283 --> 01:09:24,869
Wow, it's getting snowy now.

1589
01:09:27,288 --> 01:09:31,208
THE HIGHER THEY GET, THE SNOWIER IT GETS

1590
01:09:31,917 --> 01:09:33,127
Water's still flowing.

1591
01:09:53,397 --> 01:09:55,858
I'm too busy watching the ground
to enjoy the scenery.

1592
01:09:55,941 --> 01:09:56,859
Exactly.

1593
01:10:01,947 --> 01:10:03,699
The sound of snow is so nice.

1594
01:10:04,283 --> 01:10:05,826
-What?
-The sound of snow.

1595
01:10:05,910 --> 01:10:07,203
-It's nice.
-Right.

1596
01:10:07,286 --> 01:10:09,538
With the crampons on…

1597
01:10:09,622 --> 01:10:10,831
It's even better.

1598
01:10:13,500 --> 01:10:15,252
It's endless steps from now on.

1599
01:10:18,214 --> 01:10:19,173
Oh, dear.

1600
01:10:21,050 --> 01:10:24,345
ENDLESS ROCKY STEPS

1601
01:10:24,428 --> 01:10:28,265
THE STAFF'S PICK
1ST CRUX

1602
01:10:29,433 --> 01:10:32,853
CAR, THE GARDEN IS STILL IN THE LEAD

1603
01:10:39,985 --> 01:10:44,490
"THE MOMENT YOU OVERCOME YOURSELF,
YOU'RE AT THE TOP." -HEO YOUNG-HO

1604
01:10:48,410 --> 01:10:49,495
Geez.

1605
01:10:51,538 --> 01:10:52,623
It's killing me.

1606
01:10:56,085 --> 01:11:00,923
"THE STEEPER THE PATH,
THE HARDER MY HEART BEATS." -NIETZSCHE

1607
01:11:04,093 --> 01:11:06,053
SIGHS

1608
01:11:06,136 --> 01:11:08,514
GRUNTS

1609
01:11:10,933 --> 01:11:14,853
"IF THE SUBJECT LOOKS SMALLER,
THEY'VE FALLEN BEHIND." -HONG DEOK-HWAN

1610
01:11:15,813 --> 01:11:22,778
DIRECTOR HONG DEOK-HWAN

1611
01:11:36,292 --> 01:11:37,876
SIGHS

1612
01:11:37,960 --> 01:11:38,961
Let's go.

1613
01:11:40,170 --> 01:11:41,463
God, I'm exhausted.

1614
01:11:42,881 --> 01:11:45,676
STEPS BLOCK HIS WAY

1615
01:11:46,343 --> 01:11:47,636
SIGHS

1616
01:11:47,720 --> 01:11:49,221
Go ahead.

1617
01:11:50,222 --> 01:11:51,932
THE LEAD CHANGED

1618
01:11:52,850 --> 01:11:54,059
GRINNING

1619
01:12:12,036 --> 01:12:14,621
-We'll take a break at Gwimyeonam Rock.
-Okay.

1620
01:12:15,497 --> 01:12:17,207
STAGGERING

1621
01:12:19,126 --> 01:12:20,210
It's too tough.

1622
01:12:20,961 --> 01:12:22,296
Sit down here.

1623
01:12:22,379 --> 01:12:24,715
How about we sit down on the bench?

1624
01:12:24,798 --> 01:12:26,008
Careful.

1625
01:12:26,091 --> 01:12:27,176
Are you okay?

1626
01:12:28,177 --> 01:12:30,095
I'm okay. I'm fine.

1627
01:12:36,101 --> 01:12:37,061
Come and sit here.

1628
01:12:37,144 --> 01:12:38,437
CHECKING THE MAP MEANINGLESSLY

1629
01:12:39,730 --> 01:12:43,025
1 HOUR AND 55 MINUTES INTO HIKING
1ST BREAK

1630
01:12:43,108 --> 01:12:44,193
We can still see it.

1631
01:12:47,071 --> 01:12:48,238
This is

1632
01:12:49,406 --> 01:12:52,242
called Gwimyeonam Rock.
It was your first crux.

1633
01:12:52,951 --> 01:12:55,788
So, it's about a third of the way.

1634
01:12:56,372 --> 01:12:58,040
-Good.
-Drink some water.

1635
01:12:58,123 --> 01:13:03,170
And if you want to eat your food,
you can have it here before we move.

1636
01:13:08,675 --> 01:13:10,135
Where was the toughest?

1637
01:13:10,219 --> 01:13:11,220
Just now.

1638
01:13:16,016 --> 01:13:18,310
<i>Remember your first crux?</i>

1639
01:13:18,394 --> 01:13:21,021
When you got there, how did you feel?

1640
01:13:21,647 --> 01:13:22,773
At that point,

1641
01:13:24,483 --> 01:13:28,445
I started having the same thoughts
I'd had from the beginning.

1642
01:13:31,281 --> 01:13:34,201
"Why did I decide to do this?"

1643
01:13:34,284 --> 01:13:36,912
I usually never do something
that I know I can't do.

1644
01:13:38,705 --> 01:13:41,917
I mean, the moment you said it was hiking,
I should've walked away.

1645
01:13:42,584 --> 01:13:44,253
I mean it. Seriously.

1646
01:13:45,170 --> 01:13:46,672
It's like a slushie now.

1647
01:14:01,228 --> 01:14:02,396
Stop filming me!

1648
01:14:04,565 --> 01:14:06,442
WARNING
SLIPPERY

1649
01:14:08,193 --> 01:14:09,736
What? Your hat!

1650
01:14:10,946 --> 01:14:12,156
It blew away?

1651
01:14:24,334 --> 01:14:26,920
Some of the memories are gone, seriously.

1652
01:14:38,765 --> 01:14:40,350
<i>I really hoped he'd drop out.</i>

1653
01:14:41,477 --> 01:14:44,980
I was like,
"If he drops out, I'll do it too. Yay!"

1654
01:15:32,611 --> 01:15:34,613
Subtitle translation by: Wayne Ryu
